[2026-10-14T18:02:11.445Z] [INFO]         "output": "Critical path: every issue ends in a correct pull request or an honest failure, with any model and tool (umbrella)\n\n## Goal\n\nFor every issue Hive Mind takes, with any model (Anthropic, OpenAI or Formal AI) and any tool (`/claude`, `/codex`, `/agent`), the result is either:\n- a **correct pull request**: new commits, green CI, every requirement delivered, ready for review; or\n- an **honest failure**: reported as a failure in Telegram and on the issue or PR, with its real cause and the complete log attached, and with nothing closed that was not fixed.\n\nThis umbrella collects everything that still stops that. Each item below was checked against `main` at `d0084ee` (v2.35.10) on 2026-10-15. Production still runs 2.35.8, and the deploy is the maintainer's decision.\n\nThe same goal from the Formal AI side, with the motto \"Don't know everything, know just enough to get to know anything\", is link-assistant/formal-ai#651 → link-assistant/formal-ai#1162 / link-assistant/formal-ai#1212.\n\n## Critical blockers (sub-issues)\n\n| Issue | What breaks delivery | State on main | Open PRs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #3215 | Formal AI Hello World through `/claude`, `/codex`, `/agent` | Hive Mind side merged in #3225; live run is #3277; follow-ups #3278 and #3279 | — |\n| #3174 (+ #3276) | Link repair adds `Fixes` for sub-issues that were not implemented, including **issues in other repositories**; the merge closes them. On 2026-10-14 this closed 11 unfixed formal-ai issues. | open: `fetchRequiredIssueScope` walks every sub-issue ([L35-L55](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/d0084ee/src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs#L35-L55)) | #3175 |\n| #2406 | Auto-merge does not require evidence that each requirement was delivered | open: only the link check of #2336 shipped | #2407 |\n| #2303 | \"✅ Work session finished successfully\" after the session was OOM-killed (#3209 fixed unobserved sessions, not killed ones) | open | #2304 |\n| #2293 | Auto-restart fires on an \"issue description edited\" event that did not happen | open | #2298 |\n| #2889 | In-place kill recovery commits writable layers concurrently: ENOSPC, every recovery fails | open: no serialisation in `session-kill-resume.in-place.lib.mjs` | #2894, #2896, #3003 |\n| #2888 | Fresh kill recovery cannot resume Codex threads (per-repository `CODEX_HOME` not mounted) | open | #2893 |\n| #2891 | Kill-recovery notices posted to the parent plan PR instead of the PR being worked on | open: fallback to `sessionInfo.url` in `session-recovery-lifecycle.lib.mjs` | #2899 |\n| #2887 | Kill recovery runs the Telegram alias as the program (exit 127) | **fixed in 2.35.10** by the #2630 commits `5577dc0` and `7e1d178` (not in 2.35.8, where it still recurred on 2026-10-14). Verify after deploy, then close. The alias parts of its PRs are then superseded (#2896 also covers #2889 and #2890). | #2895, #2896, #2918, #3127 |\n| #2846 | `jq` missing in the task image: AI tools' `… \\| jq` commands exit 127 | open: not in `Dockerfile.dind`. `command -v jq` is empty in the production `hive-mind` container too. | #2852 |\n| #3176 | Repository mode selects bot-maintained status issues as work, which loops | open: `selectOldestOpenIssues` has no bot or label filter | #3179 |\n\n## Related, not blocking (not sub-issues)\n\n- #1355 / #756: one auto-restart engine and better restart comments. A refactor; the budget cap already exists.\n- #2890: persist the solve queue across restarts. Queue loss does not damage a delivered PR.\n- #2892: a daemon-restart kill is reported as OOM. A misclassification; live-restore is on now.\n- #1629 and #1610: case-study tasks for old stuck or empty sessions.\n- #3125: an auto-fix tracking instance for one OOM kill.\n\n## Done when\n\n- Every sub-issue is closed by a merged fix, and its open PRs are merged or closed as superseded.\n- #3277 passes on production, and one issue per tool and model family (Anthropic, OpenAI, Formal AI) ends in a correct PR or an honest failure as defined above.\n\nThis is a tracking umbrella: solve its sub-issues one by one. Until #3174 is fixed, a single PR for this umbrella would add `Fixes` for every sub-issue, and its merge would close them all.\n\n"
