has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"> **Status 2026-10-15: reopened. The Hive Mind side is merged, but the \"Done when\" is not met.**\n> - #3225 merged 2026-10-14 and was released as **2.35.10**, with agent pinned to 0.26.15 (link-assistant/agent#332 was fixed in agent 0.26.14). It closed #3206–#3214, #2630 and #3248.\n> - The production host still runs 2.35.8 (agent 0.26.14); the deploy is pending.\n> - #3225 itself says \"No live end-to-end run\". That run is #3277.\n> - Its known limitations are now #3278 (the remaining sync calls and lint gaps) and #3279 (Formal AI parity for `/claude` and `/codex`).\n> - The merge also **closed 11 formal-ai issues that nothing had fixed**, through the link repair's cross-repository sub-issue walk (#3276, the #3174 class). They were reopened. Their umbrella link-assistant/formal-ai#1207 was moved under link-assistant/formal-ai#1162 and is now referenced here only in text, so the next merge cannot close it again.\n> - The leftover `recovery/issue-*` branches (12, listed in #3225) are still on the remote. Deleting them needs a maintainer's OK.\n\n## Goal\n\nFormal AI is supported at every level like the OpenAI and Anthropic models: `/claude`, `/codex` and `/agent` with `--model formal-ai` each produce the simplest Hello World pull request, meeting all the requirements (new commit, green CI, ready for review), without blocking the bot or anyone else's task, and with an honest Telegram/PR report when they fail.\n\n## Runs on 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8, start-command 0.37.1, agent 0.26.13, Formal AI 0.352.1 from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8`)\n\nOptions locked for all: `--attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --isolation docker`.\n\n| Command | Session / execution | Telegram said | Reality | Log (private gist, sanitized) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `/codex …019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/issues/1` (Rust) | `67c6a8b5-28ce-48f7-ba89-8e33278f2749` / `4d45ad2c-90e8-45b7-92eb-1c63aa270972` | ✅ after 11 s, then \"⏳ Executing…\" forever | bot frozen 10 min by the image pull; 73 identical tool calls; restart iteration hit ChatGPT; exit 1, never reported | https://gist.github.com/konard/b5819c8d2e68268c18f34ba97f0b7601 |\n| `/agent …019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/issues/1` (Scala) | `435374e0-3e09-4e3d-9b8e-05f63a29093d` / `05c82f00-9417-4ebb-8c8c-97f2b893dd00` | ❌ exit 1 | a recoverable tool error was treated as fatal; Formal AI stopped and asked \"Reply `Report issue`\" | https://gist.github.com/konard/a26a79ab44357a50859a51ff7f762af6 |\n| `/claude …019fb330-fa49-7c9d-a664-b7ea33bb698a/issues/1` (Kotlin) | `e5faacab-558b-4c7d-b50c-73c4dfd61851` / `ee51df2f-6515-4273-bb9d-1785f662fbe4` | ✅ 4m 19s, PR marked ready | 2 turns, no commit by this session (false success) | https://gist.github.com/konard/150f5af4368249c49b6d20dad9f69fcf |\n\nAlso on that host the same evening: `/claude https://github.com/Godmy/stylist-svelte/issues/5`, execution `1a664acf-1a63-4973-a4a7-32fc9088c98e`: cgroup OOM, then the in-place resume exited 127 on `/claude` (#2630) and its nested dockerd did not start (#3214). Log: https://gist.github.com/konard/e4da8ea546db12107d0d4add1be34dd1\n\n## Sub-issues\n\nHive Mind:\n- #3206 bot freezes for all chats while a command prepares its task (polling stall), plus the sync-I/O audit and lint rules\n- #3207 sidecar image: remote pull before the local image, timeout reported as `unknown`, cancelled pull leaks ~17.7 GB for 6 h\n- #3208 updater/unload/fail-closed: the next Formal AI task must re-pull 7 GB of an update nobody used, or fail closed with nothing migrated\n- #3209 false \"✅ finished\" before the container existed, and the real failure never reported\n- #3210 sidecar lease kept 1 h after the task container exited\n- #3211 no-progress sessions reported as success (claude 2 turns → ready + 🎉; codex 73× loop → ✅)\n- #3212 codex auto-restart loses the Formal AI provider → ChatGPT 400 → reported as \"Authentication error\"\n- #3213 `/agent` fails on any recoverable tool error\n- #3214 stale `/var/run/docker.pid` breaks dind on in-place resume\n- #2630 kill/OOM recovery runs the Telegram alias `/claude` as a program (exit 127), still on 2.35.8 / start-command 0.37.1\n- #3248 CI: the `Formal AI Draft` workflow (`issues: opened`) failed on 53 of the last 60 issues. The root cause is the `e.g` read error chain (link-assistant/formal-ai#1189 → agent#332 → #3213), then `planned_not_executed`. The issue also covers a false \"log not attached\" comment, Formal AI cache pushed as recovery branches, no retry on the image pull, and checks not visible on the draft PR\n\nOpen follow-ups (2026-10-15):\n- #3277 live verification after deploying 2.35.10 (this issue's Done when)\n- #3278 finish #3206: 123 baselined sync calls, `require-exec-timeout` blind to `$` calls\n- #3279 Formal AI parity: attribution only with `--tool agent`, cost overrides per tool\n- #3276 (under #3174) link repair closed 11 unfixed formal-ai issues through cross-repository sub-issues\n\nDependencies:\n- link-assistant/agent#332 failed tool calls emitted as fatal top-level `error` events (fixed in agent 0.26.14)\n- link-assistant/formal-ai#1207 (text link only, see status; reopened, under link-assistant/formal-ai#1162) Formal AI side of these runs (link-assistant/formal-ai#1154, link-assistant/formal-ai#1156, link-assistant/formal-ai#1189, link-assistant/formal-ai#1205, link-assistant/formal-ai#1206) and the half-published 0.353.x release (link-assistant/formal-ai#1203, link-assistant/formal-ai#1204, link-assistant/formal-ai#1201, link-assistant/formal-ai#1153); from CI: link-assistant/formal-ai#1208 derivation records written into the user's repo, link-assistant/formal-ai#1209 `planned_not_executed` regression, link-assistant/formal-ai#1211 garbage files written and claimed as verified, and link-assistant/formal-ai#1210 the same per-issue Hive Mind draft for formal-ai's own issues\n\n## Formal AI version on the host\n\nGitHub Releases' latest is 0.352.1; 0.353.2 exists on crates.io and ghcr (`latest`) without a GitHub Release (link-assistant/formal-ai#1203). The tasks ran **0.352.1** (from the Hive Mind image). The updater pulled and accepted **0.353.2** at 23:22 UTC, no task used it, and the 5 h unload removed it at 04:10 UTC (#3208).\n\n## Done when\n\nOn a host with no Formal AI image cached, `/claude`, `/codex` and `/agent` with `--model formal-ai` on fresh Hello World test repositories (a different language each) each end with a pull request containing a new commit, green CI and a correct program, and other users' commands are answered within seconds throughout. Any failure is reported in Telegram and on the PR with its real cause. In CI, every new issue in hive-mind and formal-ai gets a Formal AI draft through Hive Mind, and its result links the complete session log (#3248, link-assistant/formal-ai#1210).\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174","id":5825265290,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWzZ-ig","number":3174,"title":"Post-session link repair adds Fixes for sub-issues a planning PR only created, and auto-merge closes them unimplemented","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-13T05:50:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T05:50:35Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":1,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"repository":{"id":1027945641,"node_id":"R_kgDOPUU0qQ","name":"hive-mind","full_name":"link-assistant/hive-mind","private":false,"owner":{"login":"link-assistant","id":245352401,"node_id":"O_kgDODp_H0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245352401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","description":"The AI that controls AIs to do the automation of automation.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Summary\n\n`solve` treats every native sub-issue of the source issue as an issue the PR must close. When the source issue asks for a **plan** (analysis plus creating implementation issues), the session attaches the implementation issues as sub-issues. From then on the post-session repair appends `Fixes #N` for each of them after **every** session, even when the agent deliberately removed those lines. Auto-merge then closes issues that were never implemented.\n\nThat is what happened in link-assistant/calculator:\n\n- PR link-assistant/calculator#228 was the plan for link-assistant/calculator#227. Its description said: `Merging this PR closes only #227. The open sub-issues #236 to #246 stay open, so this description deliberately has no Fixes lines for them.`\n- The repair appended `Fixes #229` … `Fixes #246` at 2026-10-07T10:31:07Z. The agent removed them at 10:33:43Z, and the repair re-added them at 10:44:47Z.\n- On 2026-10-12 the agent removed them twice more (19:16:26Z and 19:23:12Z). The repair re-added them at 19:40:26Z.\n- hive-mind auto-merged at 19:44:21Z. GitHub then closed link-assistant/calculator#236 to link-assistant/calculator#246, which were not implemented. They have now been reopened by hand.\n- Before the merge, the same lines made `--skip-issues-with-prs` skip every open issue in the repository (link-assistant/calculator#247, #2685).\n\nThe full timeline, every description revision and the closed events are in [docs/case-studies/issue-247](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/1b91a43a/docs/case-studies/issue-247/README.md).\n\n## Root cause (at ed6a155, v2.35.8)\n\n1. [`fetchRequiredIssueScope`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs#L34-L53) walks `…/sub_issues` recursively ([L44](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs#L44)) and marks every node as required. Nothing separates \"sub-issues to implement\" from \"sub-issues created as the plan's output\".\n2. [`repairRequiredIssueLinks`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs#L18-L44) appends a `Fixes` line for each missing one ([L32](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs#L32)). It runs in the [`finally` block](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.restart-shared.lib.mjs#L551-L555) after every session, so it always overrides the agent. It ignores a description that explicitly says the issue stays open.\n3. Auto-merge does not compare what GitHub will close (`closingIssuesReferences`) with what the PR implements.\n\n### Second problem: the shared parser and GitHub disagree on negation\n\n[`extractClosingIssueReferences`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/github-linking.lib.mjs#L38-L53) skips a keyword whose clause contains `not`, `never`, `won't` and so on. The comment there cites a PR body that said `does not close #322`. GitHub does not skip such keywords. On link-assistant/calculator#261, adding `Probe for #247: this pull request does not close #258.` made `gh pr view 261 --json closingIssuesReferences` return `[258, 260]`. Merging would have closed link-assistant/calculator#258. GitLab documents the same behaviour: https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab-foss/-/work_items/55970. So hive-mind's linking checks can say \"#N is not closed\" while the merge closes it.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe script below calls hive-mind's own `repairRequiredIssueLinks` and `extractClosingIssueReferences`, with a fake `gh` runner. It needs a checkout at ed6a155 with `npm ci --ignore-scripts --omit=dev`, then `node repro.mjs <checkout>`.\n\n<details><summary>repro.mjs</summary>\n\n```js\n// Reproduces link-assistant/calculator#247 against hive-mind's own modules.\n// Usage: node repro.mjs <path to hive-mind checkout>\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n\nconst src = (file) => pathToFileURL(resolve(process.argv[2], 'src', file)).href;\nconst { repairRequiredIssueLinks } = await import(src('pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs'));\nconst { extractClosingIssueReferences } = await import(src('github-linking.lib.mjs'));\n\n// #1 asks for a plan; #2 and #3 are the implementation issues the session\n// created and attached as native sub-issues.\nconst issues = {\n  1: \"Analyse the problem and create one issue per part of the work. This issue's own result is the analysis and the issue creation.\",\n  2: 'Implement part A.',\n  3: 'Implement part B.',\n};\nconst subIssues = { 1: [2, 3], 2: [], 3: [] };\nlet prBody = 'Closes #1\\n\\nThis PR only plans the work: #2 and #3 stay open.';\n\nconst ok = (value) => ({ code: 0, stdout: JSON.stringify(value), stderr: '' });\nconst run = async (args) => {\n  const [command, target] = args;\n  if (command === 'api' && /issues\\/\\d+\\/sub_issues$/.test(target)) {\n    const number = Number(target.split('/').at(-2));\n    return ok([subIssues[number].map((n) => ({ number: n, repository_url: 'https://api.github.com/repos/o/r' }))]);\n  }\n  if (command === 'api' && /issues\\/\\d+$/.test(target)) {\n    const number = Number(target.split('/').at(-1));\n    return ok({ number, body: issues[number] });\n  }\n  if (command === 'api' && /pulls\\/10$/.test(target)) return ok({ number: 10, body: prBody });\n  if (command === 'pr' && target === 'edit') {\n    prBody = readFileSync(args[args.indexOf('--body-file') + 1], 'utf8');\n    return { code: 0, stdout: '', stderr: '' };\n  }\n  throw new Error(`unexpected gh ${args.join(' ')}`);\n};\n\nconst repair = () => repairRequiredIssueLinks({ owner: 'o', repo: 'r', issueNumber: 1, prNumber: 10, run, logger: async (m) => console.log('  log:', m) });\n\nconsole.log('1. Session ends; the finally-block repair runs:');\nawait repair();\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(prBody));\n\nconsole.log('2. The next session removes the lines again; the repair re-adds them:');\nprBody = prBody.replace(/\\n\\n---\\n\\nFixes #2\\nFixes #3$/, '');\nawait repair();\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(prBody));\n\nconsole.log('3. hive-mind and GitHub disagree on negated keywords:');\nconst text = 'This PR does not close #2.';\nconsole.log(`  extractClosingIssueReferences(${JSON.stringify(text)}) =`, JSON.stringify(extractClosingIssueReferences(text)));\nconsole.log('  GitHub: closingIssuesReferences lists #2, and merging closes it (probe on link-assistant/calculator#261).');\n```\n\n</details>\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n1. Session ends; the finally-block repair runs:\n  log: 🔗 Repaired 2 required issue-closing reference(s) in PR #10.\n\"Closes #1\\n\\nThis PR only plans the work: #2 and #3 stay open.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFixes #2\\nFixes #3\"\n2. The next session removes the lines again; the repair re-adds them:\n  log: 🔗 Repaired 2 required issue-closing reference(s) in PR #10.\n\"Closes #1\\n\\nThis PR only plans the work: #2 and #3 stay open.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFixes #2\\nFixes #3\"\n3. hive-mind and GitHub disagree on negated keywords:\n  extractClosingIssueReferences(\"This PR does not close #2.\") = []\n  GitHub: closingIssuesReferences lists #2, and merging closes it (probe on link-assistant/calculator#261).\n```\n\n## Workarounds\n\n- In repositories hive-mind auto-merges, add a required check that fails when the description's closing keywords contradict its prose. link-assistant/calculator#261 adds one: [`scripts/check-closing-references.mjs`](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/1b91a43a/scripts/check-closing-references.mjs), run on `pull_request: [opened, edited, synchronize, reopened]`. With that check failing, hive-mind does not auto-merge.\n- For planning issues, run without auto-merge, and remove the appended lines by hand right before merging.\n- Do not write \"does not close #N\". Write \"#N stays open\" without a keyword.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. **Scope.** In `fetchRequiredIssueScope`, do not treat a native sub-issue as required when either of these holds:\n   - it was created after the PR was opened (plan output), or\n   - another PR already closes it (`closedByPullRequestsReferences`).\n\n   Keep the explicit repository-mode block (`parseRequiredClosingReferences`) and the current all-sub-issues behaviour when the parent asks for implementation, for example with an opt-in marker or flag.\n2. **Respect the description.** In `repairRequiredIssueLinks`, do not add `Fixes #N` when the body mentions `#N` without a keyword, for example in \"Part of #N\", \"#N stays open\" or \"#N to #M stay open\". Log it instead: `⚠️ #N is in the sub-issue tree but the description keeps it open; not adding a closing reference.`\n3. **Never undo the agent.** If the agent removed a reference the previous repair added, do not re-add it in the `finally` block. Report the conflict in the session summary instead.\n4. **Parser parity.** Make `extractClosingIssueReferences` return negated references, because GitHub closes them, and report them as errors (\"'does not close #N' still closes #N\"). Alternatively, use GraphQL `closingIssuesReferences` as the source of truth for repair, skip and merge checks. Before auto-merge, refuse when `closingIssuesReferences` includes an issue that is still open, is in the sub-issue tree, and has no commits in the PR (this overlaps #2406).\n5. **Regression test.** Use the link-assistant/calculator#227 wording (\"this issue's own result is the analysis and issue creation\") and assert that the implementation sub-issues created during the session are not added.\n\nRelated: #2685 / #2686 (the no-work report this caused), #2406 (complete delivery before auto-merge), #2615 (sub-issue and blocker awareness in `/hive`), #2891 (kill notices posted to the parent plan PR), link-assistant/calculator#247, link-assistant/calculator#260.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2406","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2406/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2406/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2406/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2406","id":5674958255,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABUkD9rw","number":2406,"title":"Require complete issue delivery before automated merges: prompts, Codex goals and requirements evidence","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:35:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T08:35:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"repository":{"id":1027945641,"node_id":"R_kgDOPUU0qQ","name":"hive-mind","full_name":"link-assistant/hive-mind","private":false,"owner":{"login":"link-assistant","id":245352401,"node_id":"O_kgDODp_H0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245352401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","description":"The AI that controls AIs to do the automation of automation.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"Split from #2335, as [requested on PR #2336](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2336#issuecomment-5948156787): PR #2336 keeps only the links between issues and pull requests; the prompt and goal changes move here.\n\n## Background\n\n[Agent PR #326](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/pull/326) was merged automatically after CI passed, although its own description said [Agent issue #322](https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/322) was not finished. PR #2336 fixes the link half of that incident (negated and foreign references are no longer treated as links, every required issue is linked and repaired, and the merge is blocked while a required issue link is missing or unconfirmed). A correctly linked PR can still be incomplete, which is what this issue covers.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **Prompts:** every tool (Claude, Codex, Agent, OpenCode, Gemini, Qwen) gets the same complete-delivery goal in its system, initial and continuation prompts, including the short Claude resume prompt: every requirement of every required issue must be done in the one pull request, or left explicitly unfinished.\n2. **Native goals:** where a tool supports a persistent goal, use it. For Codex, keep `features.goals=true` in both the direct and the agent-commander invocation, independently of `--auxiliary-model-calls-disabled` (the incident log shows `features.goals=false`).\n3. **Completion evidence:** a requirements report in the PR description, tied to the current head commit and to the issue/comment/review sources, listing every explicit acceptance criterion with status and evidence.\n4. **Merge guard:** automated merges of issue-scoped PRs require a current, complete report; reads fail closed, and the merge is pinned with `--match-head-commit`.\n5. **Automatic completion retries:** when the report is missing, stale or has unfinished items, continue working in the same PR with bounded retries, without needing optional restart flags.\n6. **Docs and tests:** an operating guide in all four languages, and tests with the same 100% coverage of the new modules.\n\nThe full implementation already exists as the state of PR #2336 before the split and will be opened as a pull request stacked on #2336.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.