","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","description":"The AI that controls AIs to do the automation of automation.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Problem\n\n`/solve <repository-url>` (repository mode) selects **every** open issue as work, including status pages that a bot or a scheduled workflow maintains (coverage reports, dependency dashboards, release checklists). The combined issue then requires `Fixes #<status page>` in the pull request.\n\nSuch issues are often reopened or recreated by their workflow, so this becomes a loop: the PR closes the status page, the workflow reopens it on its next run, the next repository-mode run selects it again, and another solver session spends a full run on an issue that has nothing to implement.\n\nReal case: link-assistant/calculator#258 (\"Coverage gap report\") is created and updated weekly by `github-actions[bot]`. On 2026-10-13, `/solve https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator` created link-assistant/calculator#260 with three open issues, and its required closing block contained `Fixes #258`. Until link-assistant/calculator#261, that repository's weekly workflow sent `state: 'open'` with every update, so a close would have lasted only until the next Monday.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nhive-mind `ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6` (v2.35.8), `src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs`:\n\n```js\nimport { selectOldestOpenIssues, buildCombinedIssueBody, REQUIRED_CLOSING_REFERENCES_HEADING } from './src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs';\n\nconst entries = [\n  { number: 247, id: 1, title: 'A real bug', created_at: '2026-10-08T00:00:00Z', user: { login: 'konard', type: 'User' } },\n  { number: 254, id: 2, title: 'A real feature', created_at: '2026-10-10T00:00:00Z', user: { login: 'konard', type: 'User' } },\n  { number: 258, id: 3, title: 'Coverage gap report', created_at: '2026-10-12T14:25:19Z',\n    user: { login: 'github-actions[bot]', type: 'Bot' },\n    body: '<!-- calculator:coverage-gap-report -->\\n# Coverage gap report\\n...' },\n];\nconst { selected } = selectOldestOpenIssues(entries);\nconsole.log(selected.map((issue) => issue.number)); // [ 247, 254, 258 ]\nconst body = buildCombinedIssueBody({\n  repository: { owner: 'link-assistant', repo: 'calculator', fullName: 'link-assistant/calculator', url: 'https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator' },\n  issues: selected, totalOpen: entries.length, attachmentCount: selected.length,\n});\nconsole.log(body.slice(body.indexOf(REQUIRED_CLOSING_REFERENCES_HEADING)));\n// ```\n// Fixes #247\n// Fixes #254\n// Fixes #258   <- the bot-maintained status page\n// ```\n```\n\nThe full script and its output: https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/09410d73/experiments/issue-258/hive-mind-dashboard-selection-repro.mjs and https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/09410d73/docs/case-studies/issue-258/data/hive-mind-dashboard-selection-repro.txt\n\n## Root cause\n\n- [`selectOldestOpenIssues`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs#L109-L131) filters out only pull requests. It accepts an `exclude` list of issue numbers, but [`prepareRepositoryModeIssue`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.repository-mode.run.lib.mjs#L137-L141) never passes it, and no CLI option sets it.\n- Nothing looks at labels, the author type, or a body marker, so a repository cannot say \"this issue is not work\".\n- [`buildCombinedIssueBody`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs) puts every selected issue in the required closing block. Combined with the post-session link repair (#3174), the pull request ends up closing the status page whatever the agent decides.\n\n## Workarounds\n\n- In the repository: make the status workflow update its issue without reopening it, so one close sticks. Example: https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/pull/261 (`scripts/update-coverage-gap-issue.mjs` no longer sends `state`; the body lists the issues that track the actual work).\n- Close the status page as \"not planned\" before running repository mode, if its workflow does not reopen it.\n- Solve the real issues one by one (`/solve <issue-url>`) instead of using repository mode.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. **Let a repository opt issues out.** Skip open issues that carry a label from a configurable list (for example `--skip-issue-labels`, defaulting to something like `hive-mind:skip`, `dashboard`, `status`) or a body marker such as `<!-- hive-mind:skip -->`. Pass the result through the existing `exclude` option of `selectOldestOpenIssues`.\n2. **Treat bot-authored issues as opt-in, or at least flag them.** Issues with `user.type === 'Bot'` are mostly reports and dashboards (Renovate's \"Dependency Dashboard\", coverage and benchmark reports). Either skip them unless a flag includes them, or keep them but list them separately in the combined issue (\"maintained by a bot, close only if the PR changes what it reports\").\n3. **Show what was left out.** `buildCombinedIssueBody` already reports issues over the sub-issue limit. Add a line for issues skipped by label, marker or author, with the reason, so the scope stays reviewable.\n4. **Regression tests.** `selectOldestOpenIssues` with a labeled issue, a marked issue and a bot-authored issue. `prepareRepositoryModeIssue` passing the exclusions. The combined body listing the skipped issues and leaving them out of the closing block.\n\nRelated: #3174 (post-session link repair re-adds `Fixes` lines for the whole sub-issue tree).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","id":5842395156,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDvgFA","number":3215,"title":"Formal AI Hello World via /claude, /codex, /agent (2026-10-13, 2.35.8): every run failed or falsely succeeded — umbrella (sub-issues)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:19:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:47:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":15,"completed":12,"percent_completed":80},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> **Status 2026-10-15: reopened. The Hive Mind side is merged, but the \"Done when\" is not met.**\n> - #3225 merged 2026-10-14 and was released as **2.35.10**, with agent pinned to 0.26.15 (link-assistant/agent#332 was fixed in agent 0.26.14). It closed #3206–#3214, #2630 and #3248.\n> - The production host still runs 2.35.8 (agent 0.26.14); the deploy is pending.\n> - #3225 itself says \"No live end-to-end run\". That run is #3277.\n> - Its known limitations are now #3278 (the remaining sync calls and lint gaps) and #3279 (Formal AI parity for `/claude` and `/codex`).\n> - The merge also **closed 11 formal-ai issues that nothing had fixed**, through the link repair's cross-repository sub-issue walk (#3276, the #3174 class). They were reopened. Their umbrella link-assistant/formal-ai#1207 was moved under link-assistant/formal-ai#1162 and is now referenced here only in text, so the next merge cannot close it again.\n> - The leftover `recovery/issue-*` branches (12, listed in #3225) are still on the remote. Deleting them needs a maintainer's OK.\n\n## Goal\n\nFormal AI is supported at every level like the OpenAI and Anthropic models: `/claude`, `/codex` and `/agent` with `--model formal-ai` each produce the simplest Hello World pull request, meeting all the requirements (new commit, green CI, ready for review), without blocking the bot or anyone else's task, and with an honest Telegram/PR report when they fail.\n\n## Runs on 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8, start-command 0.37.1, agent 0.26.13, Formal AI 0.352.1 from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8`)\n\nOptions locked for all: `--attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --isolation docker`.\n\n| Command | Session / execution | Telegram said | Reality | Log (private gist, sanitized) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `/codex …019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/issues/1` (Rust) | `67c6a8b5-28ce-48f7-ba89-8e33278f2749` / `4d45ad2c-90e8-45b7-92eb-1c63aa270972` | ✅ after 11 s, then \"⏳ Executing…\" forever | bot frozen 10 min by the image pull; 73 identical tool calls; restart iteration hit ChatGPT; exit 1, never reported | https://gist.github.com/konard/b5819c8d2e68268c18f34ba97f0b7601 |\n| `/agent …019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/issues/1` (Scala) | `435374e0-3e09-4e3d-9b8e-05f63a29093d` / `05c82f00-9417-4ebb-8c8c-97f2b893dd00` | ❌ exit 1 | a recoverable tool error was treated as fatal; Formal AI stopped and asked \"Reply `Report issue`\" | https://gist.github.com/konard/a26a79ab44357a50859a51ff7f762af6 |\n| `/claude …019fb330-fa49-7c9d-a664-b7ea33bb698a/issues/1` (Kotlin) | `e5faacab-558b-4c7d-b50c-73c4dfd61851` / `ee51df2f-6515-4273-bb9d-1785f662fbe4` | ✅ 4m 19s, PR marked ready | 2 turns, no commit by this session (false success) | https://gist.github.com/konard/150f5af4368249c49b6d20dad9f69fcf |\n\nAlso on that host the same evening: `/claude https://github.com/Godmy/stylist-svelte/issues/5`, execution `1a664acf-1a63-4973-a4a7-32fc9088c98e`: cgroup OOM, then the in-place resume exited 127 on `/claude` (#2630) and its nested dockerd did not start (#3214). Log: https://gist.github.com/konard/e4da8ea546db12107d0d4add1be34dd1\n\n## Sub-issues\n\nHive Mind:\n- #3206 bot freezes for all chats while a command prepares its task (polling stall), plus the sync-I/O audit and lint rules\n- #3207 sidecar image: remote pull before the local image, timeout reported as `unknown`, cancelled pull leaks ~17.7 GB for 6 h\n- #3208 updater/unload/fail-closed: the next Formal AI task must re-pull 7 GB of an update nobody used, or fail closed with nothing migrated\n- #3209 false \"✅ finished\" before the container existed, and the real failure never reported\n- #3210 sidecar lease kept 1 h after the task container exited\n- #3211 no-progress sessions reported as success (claude 2 turns → ready + 🎉; codex 73× loop → ✅)\n- #3212 codex auto-restart loses the Formal AI provider → ChatGPT 400 → reported as \"Authentication error\"\n- #3213 `/agent` fails on any recoverable tool error\n- #3214 stale `/var/run/docker.pid` breaks dind on in-place resume\n- #2630 kill/OOM recovery runs the Telegram alias `/claude` as a program (exit 127), still on 2.35.8 / start-command 0.37.1\n- #3248 CI: the `Formal AI Draft` workflow (`issues: opened`) failed on 53 of the last 60 issues. The root cause is the `e.g` read error chain (link-assistant/formal-ai#1189 → agent#332 → #3213), then `planned_not_executed`. The issue also covers a false \"log not attached\" comment, Formal AI cache pushed as recovery branches, no retry on the image pull, and checks not visible on the draft PR\n\nOpen follow-ups (2026-10-15):\n- #3277 live verification after deploying 2.35.10 (this issue's Done when)\n- #3278 finish #3206: 123 baselined sync calls, `require-exec-timeout` blind to `$` calls\n- #3279 Formal AI parity: attribution only with `--tool agent`, cost overrides per tool\n- #3276 (under #3174) link repair closed 11 unfixed formal-ai issues through cross-repository sub-issues\n\nDependencies:\n- link-assistant/agent#332 failed tool calls emitted as fatal top-level `error` events (fixed in agent 0.26.14)\n- link-assistant/formal-ai#1207 (text link only, see status; reopened, under link-assistant/formal-ai#1162) Formal AI side of these runs (link-assistant/formal-ai#1154, link-assistant/formal-ai#1156, link-assistant/formal-ai#1189, link-assistant/formal-ai#1205, link-assistant/formal-ai#1206) and the half-published 0.353.x release (link-assistant/formal-ai#1203, link-assistant/formal-ai#1204, link-assistant/formal-ai#1201, link-assistant/formal-ai#1153); from CI: link-assistant/formal-ai#1208 derivation records written into the user's repo, link-assistant/formal-ai#1209 `planned_not_executed` regression, link-assistant/formal-ai#1211 garbage files written and claimed as verified, and link-assistant/formal-ai#1210 the same per-issue Hive Mind draft for formal-ai's own issues\n\n## Formal AI version on the host\n\nGitHub Releases' latest is 0.352.1; 0.353.2 exists on crates.io and ghcr (`latest`) without a GitHub Release (link-assistant/formal-ai#1203). The tasks ran **0.352.1** (from the Hive Mind image). The updater pulled and accepted **0.353.2** at 23:22 UTC, no task used it, and the 5 h unload removed it at 04:10 UTC (#3208).\n\n## Done when\n\nOn a host with no Formal AI image cached, `/claude`, `/codex` and `/agent` with `--model formal-ai` on fresh Hello World test repositories (a different language each) each end with a pull request containing a new commit, green CI and a correct program, and other users' commands are answered within seconds throughout. Any failure is reported in Telegram and on the PR with its real cause. In CI, every new issue in hive-mind and formal-ai gets a Formal AI draft through Hive Mind, and its result links the complete session log (#3248, link-assistant/formal-ai#1210).\n\n\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null}[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206","id":5842383598,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDuy7g","number":3206,"title":"Telegram bot freezes for all chats while a command prepares its task: /codex --model formal-ai blocked polling for 10 min (handlerTimeout: Infinity + awaited image pull); sync I/O audit and lint rules","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:17:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:34Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:34Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"repository":{"id":1027945641,"node_id":"R_kgDOPUU0qQ","name":"hive-mind","full_name":"link-assistant/hive-mind","private":false,"owner":{"login":"link-assistant","id":245352401,"node_id":"O_kgDODp_H0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245352401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","description":"The AI that controls AIs to do the automation of automation.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Problem\n\nA single `/codex … --model formal-ai` request froze the whole Telegram bot for **10 minutes** on 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8):\n\n- 21:52:05 UTC: the `/codex` handler started `docker pull ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai:0.352.1` (via `ensureFormalAiSidecarImage`, awaited inside the update handler).\n- **No `getUpdates` call between 21:51:34 and 22:02:16 UTC.** Every other user's command in every chat waited.\n- 22:02:05: the pull was killed by `DEFAULT_DOCKER_TIMEOUT_MS = 600_000` (`src/formal-ai-image.lib.mjs:65`), and the bot then fell back to the local `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8` image that was on the host all along (tracked in the pull sub-issue).\n\nRoot cause: `src/telegram-bot.mjs:212` sets `handlerTimeout: Infinity`, and Telegraf's long polling does not request the next batch until every handler of the current batch has resolved. The `/solve`/`/codex`/`/agent`/`/claude` handler `await`s `executeAndUpdateMessage(...)` (`telegram-bot.mjs:707`, `/hive` at `:883`, `/fix` in `telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs:233`, `/task` in `telegram-task-command.lib.mjs:311`), and that awaits the Formal AI image resolution, sidecar start and `$ --isolated docker` launch.\n\nInstalling or updating Formal AI (or any other slow preparation) must never block other bot operations.\n\n## Audit (main `a8bec06`, 2.35.9)\n\n**Long awaits inside update handlers** (each stalls *all* chats while it runs):\n\n| Handler | Where | Await | Typical |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| /solve, /codex, /agent, /claude, /hive, /fix, /task | `telegram-bot.mjs:707`, `:883`, `telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs:233`, `telegram-task-command.lib.mjs:311` | `executeAndUpdateMessage` → Formal AI image pull / sidecar start / container launch | seconds; **up to 10 min** on a cold Formal AI host |\n| /solve | `telegram-bot.mjs:641`, `:647`, `:666` | `validateGitHubEntityExistence`, `autoAcceptInviteForRepo`, `preflightRepositoryTarget` (sequential `gh api`) | 1–10 s |\n| /accept_invites | `telegram-accept-invitations.lib.mjs:185`, `:191` | `gh api … --paginate` | 1–30 s |\n| /merge | `telegram-merge-command.lib.mjs:329`, `:336`, `:420` | label checks, `processor.initialize()` | 1–10 s |\n\n**Synchronous I/O in the bot process** (blocks the event loop, so also polling, timers and other handlers):\n\n- `eslint-plugin-n` `n/no-sync` over `src/`: **141** calls in 25 files (many are CLI-only and fine).\n- In modules the bot loads: `bot-logger.lib.mjs` (9: `statSync` + `appendFileSync` on **every** log line, rotation with `renameSync`/`readdirSync`/`unlinkSync`), `lib.mjs:350-351` (`appendFileSync`/`chmodSync` in the stdout/stderr interceptor, on every console write), `session-store.lib.mjs` (5, `appendFileSync` per session event), `model-catalogue.lib.mjs` (4, `readFileSync` in the `/models` path), `docker-sidecar.lib.mjs` (4), `state-lock.lib.mjs` (5, a `mkdir` lock: legitimate, mark it), `isolation-runner.lib.mjs` (10), `session-resume.lib.mjs` (6), `router-session-drain.lib.mjs` (5), `agentic-cli-updater.lib.mjs` (4), `solve.disk-diagnostics.lib.mjs:50,63` (`execFileSync('du')`, reached from `session-monitor` on session completion: a `du` over a large workspace blocks the bot).\n- **60** `docker`/`git`/`gh` child processes started without a `timeout` (14 files; `github-merge.lib.mjs` 27, `github-merge-ci-signals.lib.mjs` 5, `telegram-accept-invitations.lib.mjs` 4, `solve.accept-invite.lib.mjs` 4, …).\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Handlers return immediately.** A command handler validates, replies \"Starting…\", and hands the launch to a background job (`void launch(...).catch(report)`), whose progress and errors edit that message. Image pulls, sidecar start and container launch never run on the update path.\n2. Replace `handlerTimeout: Infinity` with a finite value (Telegraf's 90 s default or less) **after** (1), so a regression shows up as a logged handler timeout instead of a frozen bot.\n3. A runtime watchdog: wrap every registered handler and log a warning (and a counter in the heartbeat) when one runs longer than 2 s. This catches transitive blocking that lint cannot see.\n4. Make the bot's hot paths async: a `fs.createWriteStream` logger (no `statSync`/`appendFileSync` per line), async session-store appends, async `du`.\n5. Lint rules, so this does not come back:\n   - `n/no-sync` (eslint-plugin-n, industry standard) as `error` for every module reachable from `src/telegram-bot.mjs` (compute the import closure in the config, rather than a filename list), with `// hive-sync-ok: <reason>` for startup-only and exit-handler code.\n   - `no-await-in-loop` (core) as `warn`.\n   - `promise/catch-or-return` (eslint-plugin-promise), so the fire-and-forget launches in (1) always handle rejection. (`@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` needs type information; this repository is plain ESM JS.)\n   - No industry rule covers the two Hive-Mind-specific patterns, so add custom rules (drafts, tested against `main`, private gist: https://gist.github.com/konard/e621dc37520a2ab7e64a006f0832e3c7):\n     - `hive/require-exec-timeout`: every `exec`/`execFile`/`spawn` (sync or async) of `docker`, `git` or `gh` passes a `timeout` (60 findings today).\n     - `hive/no-slow-await-in-telegram-handler`: no `await` of a known-slow function (`ensureFormalAiSidecarImage`, `executeAndUpdateMessage`, `validateGitHubEntityExistence`, `sleep`, …) inside a function registered with `bot.command`/`bot.on`/`bot.hears`. The draft finds 0 today because handlers are registered by name; the rule must resolve the identifier to its declaration (scope analysis) to close that gap.\n     - `hive/no-sync-in-bot-process`: the import-closure scoping of `n/no-sync` above (27 findings with the draft's filename list).\n6. A regression test: with `docker pull` stubbed to hang, a `/codex … --model formal-ai` update must not delay the handling of a second update (e.g. `/help`) by more than 1 s.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207","id":5842383815,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDuzxw","number":3207,"title":"Formal AI sidecar image: pulls 6.2 GB from ghcr before using the local Hive Mind image with the same version, 600 s timeout reported as 'unknown', cancelled pull leaks ~17.7 GB for 6 h","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https: