ved_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-09-25T15:04:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T09:36:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":29937030,"node_id":"IT_kwDODp_H0c4ByM2G","name":"Bug","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","color":"red","created_at":"2025-11-21T09:35:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T09:35:16Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/pull/184#issuecomment-5824973158 (issue description)\n- https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/pull/184#issuecomment-5832445399 (issue description and title)\n\nIn both cases I see original https://github.com/link-foundation/relative-meta-logic/issues/183 and it has exactly 0 changes in the history.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2293/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889","id":5780053948,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWISfvA","number":2889,"title":"In-place kill recovery commits whole task writable layers concurrently, filling the disk (ENOSPC) and loading CPU for 30+ minutes","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:50:19Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:13:22Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Incident context (2026-10-09)\n\nHost: Ubuntu 24.04, 6 CPU, 11.7 GB RAM, 193 GB disk, Docker 29.6.1 with the containerd image store (`overlayfs` snapshotter), live-restore disabled. Root container `hive-mind` (DinD variant, `--restart unless-stopped`) runs `hive-telegram-bot`; tasks run as `$ --isolated docker` containers from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.34.0`. hive-mind 2.34.0, start-command 0.35.4.\n\nAt 12:11:39 UTC the kernel OOM-killed the **host dockerd** (7.3 GB RSS, caused by ~22 concurrent `docker diff` calls from a disk-cleanup tool test suite run inside the root container — link-foundation/disk-space-saviour#22). systemd restarted dockerd, which SIGKILLed every running container (exit 137): the root `hive-mind` container and four `/codex` solve tasks for link-assistant/router#724, #725, #727, #728. The root container was started again manually at 13:31 UTC; the bot then ran its built-in kill recovery.\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter a host-wide kill, the bot recovers every killed session in place at about the same time (random delays of 34–73 s, #2498). Each in-place recovery is `$ --resume` in `docker-snapshot` mode, i.e. `docker commit` of the **whole writable layer** of the killed task container. With four Rust tasks that was 11 + 21.2 + 23.5 + 36.8 GiB, almost all of it Cargo `target/` directories (8.6 + 18 + 17 + 31 GB), on a host with 52 GB free.\n\nObserved:\n- 4 commits ran concurrently; containerd used ~280 % CPU for 30+ minutes, compressing layers.\n- Free disk went 52 GB → 2 GB; the host reached 96 % used.\n- router#727's commit failed: `failed to apply diff: write /var/lib/containerd/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/7124/fs/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791515915848/target/debug/deps/link_assistant_router-…: no space left on device`; router#725's commit failed the same way. Both fell back to fresh runs that failed (#2888).\n- Every successful snapshot is a full copy: the original container (11 / 23.5 GiB) and the `start-command-resume/<name>:1` image (46.7 / 62.7 GB including the base) coexist until someone removes the original by hand.\n- Even a ~560 KiB layer takes 10+ minutes to commit: with the containerd image store, commit computes the diff by walking the full mounted filesystem.\n\n## Expected\n\nRecovery never fills the disk it needs to keep working, and does not duplicate tens of GB of regenerable build output.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- **Avoid the copy:** make the task container resumable with `docker start` (`ResumeMode.DOCKER_START`, no commit). For example, have the launch command read the command to run from a file in the container (written by the bot before `docker start`), so the same container can re-run with `--resume <id>`. Today `docker start` would re-run the gate loop `while [ ! -e \"$gate\" ]` for a gate file that was already deleted and hang.\n- **If a snapshot is needed:** preflight free disk against the container's writable-layer size (with headroom for the compressed blob plus the unpacked snapshot), run snapshots **one at a time**, and drop regenerable caches first (Cargo `target/`, `node_modules/.cache`, …) or exclude them.\n- After a snapshot-derived container starts successfully, remove the original stopped container (its data is in the image) and remove obsolete `start-command-resume/*` images after the task finishes.\n- Report the state in Telegram (`waiting for disk`, `snapshotting 12/37 GiB`) instead of failing silently.\n\n---\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\n\nRelated: #2887 (resumed command is the Telegram alias), #2888 (fresh fallback cannot resume Codex threads).\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2889/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888","id":5780053446,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWISdxg","number":2888,"title":"Fresh-run kill recovery cannot resume Codex threads: per-repository CODEX_HOME is not mounted into task containers (no rollout found for thread id)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:50:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T14:52:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Incident context (2026-10-09)\n\nHost: Ubuntu 24.04, 6 CPU, 11.7 GB RAM, 193 GB disk, Docker 29.6.1 with the containerd image store (`overlayfs` snapshotter), live-restore disabled. Root container `hive-mind` (DinD variant, `--restart unless-stopped`) runs `hive-telegram-bot`; tasks run as `$ --isolated docker` containers from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.34.0`. hive-mind 2.34.0, start-command 0.35.4.\n\nAt 12:11:39 UTC the kernel OOM-killed the **host dockerd** (7.3 GB RSS, caused by ~22 concurrent `docker diff` calls from a disk-cleanup tool test suite run inside the root container — link-foundation/disk-space-saviour#22). systemd restarted dockerd, which SIGKILLed every running container (exit 137): the root `hive-mind` container and four `/codex` solve tasks for link-assistant/router#724, #725, #727, #728. The root container was started again manually at 13:31 UTC; the bot then ran its built-in kill recovery.\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen in-place recovery is not possible, the fresh-run fallback launches `solve … --resume <codex thread id>` in a **new** task container. For Codex that can never work: the thread's rollout is stored in the killed container's own filesystem, so the new run fails within a minute and posts a failure on the PR.\n\nrouter#727, fallback session `78dcf29e-8ee2-40f5-aca5-2e967ac692af` (comments https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/752#issuecomment-6082862406 and https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/752#issuecomment-6082869911):\n```\nWarning: Session log for 01a11f62-7b6a-7443-b4e1-c66d343b6915 not found, but continuing with resume attempt\nCreating temporary directory for resumed session: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-resume-01a11f62-…\n(export CODEX_HOME=/home/box/.codex/hive-mind/repositories/link-assistant/router; … codex exec resume \"01a11f62-7b6a-7443-b4e1-c66d343b6915\" …)\nError: thread/resume: thread/resume failed: no rollout found for thread id 01a11f62-7b6a-7443-b4e1-c66d343b6915 (code -32600)\n❌ CODEX execution failed\n```\n\nThe same task resumed **in place** (snapshot of the killed container, router#728) found its thread: `{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a1200a-276e-76b2-9674-c219f0f54121\"}`.\n\nA second fallback (router#725, `f648b389-…`) did not even start: `❌ Insufficient disk space on this host (10215MB available, 10240MB required) — the issue itself was not attempted` (exit 75), and it still consumed recovery attempt 1/3.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- solve runs Codex with a per-repository `CODEX_HOME` built by [`buildCodexCapabilityStatePath`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/codex-capability-preflight.lib.mjs#L162-L164): `~/.codex/hive-mind/repositories/<owner>/<repo>`. Rollouts for the thread are written there.\n- Task containers only bind-mount `~/.codex/auth.json` and `~/.codex/sessions` (from `$ --list`: `\"volumes\": [\"/home/box/.config/gh:…\", \"/home/box/.gitconfig:…\", \"/home/box/.codex/auth.json:…\", \"/home/box/.codex/sessions:…\"]`), so the per-repository home dies with the container.\n- [`startKillRecoverySession`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/session-kill-resume.lib.mjs#L163) launches the fresh run with `plan.command.args`, which always include `--resume <id>`.\n\n## Expected\n\nA fresh recovery run either has the thread available or does not ask for it.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. Before the fresh launch, copy the thread's rollout out of the stopped container (`docker cp <killed>:<CODEX_HOME> …` works on stopped containers) and make it available to the new container (mount or copy into its `CODEX_HOME`), or persist the per-repository `CODEX_HOME` on a mounted volume in the first place.\n2. If the rollout cannot be recovered, launch without `--resume` (`--auto-continue` on the existing PR) instead of a run that is guaranteed to fail.\n3. A launch refused by the disk preflight (exit 75, nothing attempted) should not count as a recovery attempt and should be retried when space frees up.\n4. Check the same for every tool with `--resume` (claude, agent, gemini, qwen): where does each keep its session, and is it mounted into task containers?\n\n---\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2888/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891","id":5780054956,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWISjrA","number":2891,"title":"Kill recovery notices are posted to the wrong pull request (first linked PR, e.g. the parent plan PR)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:50:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T14:52:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Incident context (2026-10-09)\n\nHost: Ubuntu 24.04, 6 CPU, 11.7 GB RAM, 193 GB disk, Docker 29.6.1 with the containerd image store (`overlayfs` snapshotter), live-restore disabled. Root container `hive-mind` (DinD variant, `--restart unless-stopped`) runs `hive-telegram-bot`; tasks run as `$ --isolated docker` containers from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.34.0`. hive-mind 2.34.0, start-command 0.35.4.\n\nAt 12:11:39 UTC the kernel OOM-killed the **host dockerd** (7.3 GB RSS, caused by ~22 concurrent `docker diff` calls from a disk-cleanup tool test suite run inside the root container — link-foundation/disk-space-saviour#22). systemd restarted dockerd, which SIGKILLed every running container (exit 137): the root `hive-mind` container and four `/codex` solve tasks for link-assistant/router#724, #725, #727, #728. The root container was started again manually at 13:31 UTC; the bot then ran its built-in kill recovery.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe kill-recovery lifecycle notices for four different tasks were all posted to **link-assistant/router#721**, an unrelated PR, instead of each task's own PR:\n\n| Task | Own PR | Notice posted to |\n|---|---|---|\n| router#724 | #749 (`issue-724-878028a21e67`) | https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/721#issuecomment-6081947908 |\n| router#725 | #750 (`issue-725-052105988e50`) | https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/721#issuecomment-6081957476 |\n| router#727 | #752 (`issue-727-61ea612f008e`) | https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/721#issuecomment-6081964840 |\n| router#728 | #753 (`issue-728-9679a13cda3c`) | https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/721#issuecomment-6081974137 |\n\n#721 is the case-study PR for issue #720 (`issue-720-99e7abc4e6c1`), which plans those sub-issues.\n\n## Root cause\n\nGitHub links **both** PRs to each sub-issue:\n```\ngh api graphql … issue(number:724){ closedByPullRequestsReferences … }\n→ [{number:721, headRefName:\"issue-720-99e7abc4e6c1\"}, {number:749, headRefName:\"issue-724-878028a21e67\"}]\n```\n[`resolvePullRequestUrlForSession`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/session-monitor.lib.mjs#L1076-L1110) returns `linkedPRs[0].url` without checking which PR belongs to the session. The session log fallback ([`resolvePullRequestUrlFromSessionLog`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/session-monitor.lib.mjs#L358-L377)) returns the first `/pull/N` URL it meets, so it can pick a PR the agent merely mentioned.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- Prefer the PR the session itself created/used: the branch `issue-<n>-*` solve printed, or the PR URL from solve's structured output, stored in `sessionInfo` when the session starts.\n- Among linked PRs, pick the one whose head branch matches `issue-<n>-`; never a PR whose branch belongs to another issue.\n- Apply the same selection everywhere a PR is resolved for a session (completion messages, kill notices, log attachments).\n\n---\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2891/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887","id":5780052996,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWIScBA","number":2887,"title":"Kill recovery runs the Telegram alias as the program (sh: /codex: not found, exit 127), then reports the task as oom-killed","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:50:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:55:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> **Status 2026-10-15:** the same bug as #2630. It is fixed in **2.35.10** by commits `5577dc0` (\"execute solve for alias recovery\") and `7e1d178`, which are not in 2.35.8. Production still runs 2.35.8, which is why the auto-fix reports of 2026-10-14 still show it. Close this after a kill recovery on 2.35.10 is observed to run `solve` (#3277). Then the alias parts of the open PRs #2895, #2918 and #3127 are superseded. #2896 also covers #2889 and #2890. Tracked in #3282.\n\n## Incident context (2026-10-09)\n\nHost: Ubuntu 24.04, 6 CPU, 11.7 GB RAM, 193 GB disk, Docker 29.6.1 with the containerd image store (`overlayfs` snapshotter), live-restore disabled. Root container `hive-mind` (DinD variant, `--restart unless-stopped`) runs `hive-telegram-bot`; tasks run as `$ --isolated docker` containers from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.34.0`. hive-mind 2.34.0, start-command 0.35.4.\n\nAt 12:11:39 UTC the kernel OOM-killed the **host dockerd** (7.3 GB RSS, caused by ~22 concurrent `docker diff` calls from a disk-cleanup tool test suite run inside the root container — link-foundation/disk-space-saviour#22). systemd restarted dockerd, which SIGKILLed every running container (exit 137): the root `hive-mind` container and four `/codex` solve tasks for link-assistant/router#724, #725, #727, #728. The root container was started again manually at 13:31 UTC; the bot then ran its built-in kill recovery.\n\n## Problem\n\nIn-place kill recovery (`$ --resume <execution> -- <command>`) runs the **Telegram command alias as the shell program**. Every recovered `/codex` task fails instantly with exit 127, and the bot then reports it as `oom-killed` and stops tracking it.\n\n```\n$ docker logs eec34a2b-aa97-4bf1-8879-b483ab13d784-resume-1\n[dind-entrypoint] Starting dockerd (storage-driver=fuse-overlayfs, data-root=/var/lib/docker)\n[dind-entrypoint] dockerd is ready after 1s\n[dind-entrypoint] image preload/passthrough complete\nsh: 1: /codex: not found\n\n$ docker inspect -f '{{json .Config.Cmd}}' eec34a2b-aa97-4bf1-8879-b483ab13d784-resume-1\n[\"sh\",\"-c\",\"/codex https://github.com/link-assistant/router/issues/728 --think xhigh --auto-merge --tool codex --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en --resume 01a1200a-276e-76b2-9674-c219f0f54121\"]\n```\n\nThe same happened to router#724 (`9243e682-…-resume-1`, exit 127). Each of these attempts first spent 10–35 minutes and 11–24 GB of disk on `docker commit` of the killed container, only to run a command that cannot exist.\n\nBot log afterwards (wrong status, session dropped):\n```\nEVENT session_completion_notified {\"sessionName\":\"eec34a2b-aa97-4bf1-8879-b483ab13d784\",\"exitCode\":137,\"status\":\"oom-killed\",...}\n[VERBOSE] Session eec34a2b-aa97-4bf1-8879-b483ab13d784 removed from tracking (exit: 137, status: oom-killed)\n```\nThe resumed container exited **127**, not 137, but the record kept the old `OOMKilled=true`/137 diagnosis.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- [`buildResumeCommand`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/session-resume.lib.mjs#L256-L274) uses `/${commandAlias}` as the binary when the task came from a Telegram alias (L263-L264). That string is meant for copy-paste into Telegram (#2109), not for a shell.\n- [`resumeKilledSessionInPlace`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/session-kill-resume.in-place.lib.mjs#L197) passes `plan.command.display` as the command `$ --resume` runs inside the container.\n- The fresh-run fallback ([session-kill-resume.lib.mjs#L163](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/790c18dec9ec0dd2281de05a48f2047690a60415/src/session-kill-resume.lib.mjs#L163)) uses `sessionInfo.command` + `args`, so it is not affected — only the in-place path is.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. `/codex https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>` in Telegram (docker isolation).\n2. `docker kill <task container>` while the tool is running.\n3. Wait for the kill recovery: the `<name>-resume-1` container exits 127 with `sh: 1: /codex: not found`.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe in-place command is the executable (`solve …` / `hive …`) with the original args plus `--resume <last tool session id>`. The alias form stays only in user-facing text. A resumed container's own exit code/reason is reported (127, \"command not found\"), not the killed predecessor's.\n\n## Workaround (verified)\n\nRe-run the resume with the real program; the snapshot already exists, so this is cheap:\n```\n$ --resume deb9c2e9-8234-43ef-9648-e102f5d34ebd --output-format json -- \\\n  solve https://github.com/link-assistant/router/issues/728 --think xhigh --auto-merge --tool codex \\\n  --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en \\\n  --resume 01a1200a-276e-76b2-9674-c219f0f54121\n```\nResult: `eec34a2b-…-resume-1-resume-2` started, and Codex resumed the original thread (`{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a1200a-276e-76b2-9674-c219f0f54121\"}`).\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- Give `buildResumeCommand` separate `display` (alias, for Telegram/PR text) and `shell` (executable) forms, and use the executable form in every place that runs a command (`$ --resume`, `executeWithIsolation`, any `recoveryCommand`).\n- Add a test that the in-place resume command never starts with `/`.\n- When a resumed container exits, classify it from its own exit (127 → \"command not found\", not `oom-killed`) and keep tracking/recovering instead of dropping the session.\n\n---\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\n\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2887/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846","id":5776019172,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWEcO5A","number":2846,"title":"jq missing from konard/hive-mind-dind image (exit 127)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-09T09:36:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T09:36:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n`jq` is missing from `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.34.0`. AI tools and hive-mind's own printed commands use it:\n```\n⚠️ Tool result error detected: Exit code 127\njq: command not found\n```\n- Seen in link-assistant/web-capture#178: Claude's `… | jq -r …` failed, and Claude fell back to `gh --jq`.\n- hive-mind's own \"Raw command\" printout also pipes through `| jq -c .`.\n\n## Expected\nAdd `jq` to the image (and to the image verification list), the same way #2687 / PR #2690 added `file`.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2846/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176","id":5825421120,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWzjfQA","number":3176,"title":"Repository mode selects bot-maintained status issues (reports, dashboards) as work, with no way to exclude them","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-13T06:05:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T06:05:57Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\n`/solve <repository-url>` (repository mode) selects **every** open issue as work, including status pages that a bot or a scheduled workflow maintains (coverage reports, dependency dashboards, release checklists). The combined issue then requires `Fixes #<status page>` in the pull request.\n\nSuch issues are often reopened or recreated by their workflow, so this becomes a loop: the PR closes the status page, the workflow reopens it on its next run, the next repository-mode run selects it again, and another solver session spends a full run on an issue that has nothing to implement.\n\nReal case: link-assistant/calculator#258 (\"Coverage gap report\") is created and updated weekly by `github-actions[bot]`. On 2026-10-13, `/solve https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator` created link-assistant/calculator#260 with three open issues, and its required closing block contained `Fixes #258`. Until link-assistant/calculator#261, that repository's weekly workflow sent `state: 'open'` with every update, so a close would have lasted only until the next Monday.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nhive-mind `ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6` (v2.35.8), `src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs`:\n\n```js\nimport { selectOldestOpenIssues, buildCombinedIssueBody, REQUIRED_CLOSING_REFERENCES_HEADING } from './src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs';\n\nconst entries = [\n  { number: 247, id: 1, title: 'A real bug', created_at: '2026-10-08T00:00:00Z', user: { login: 'konard', type: 'User' } },\n  { number: 254, id: 2, title: 'A real feature', created_at: '2026-10-10T00:00:00Z', user: { login: 'konard', type: 'User' } },\n  { number: 258, id: 3, title: 'Coverage gap report', created_at: '2026-10-12T14:25:19Z',\n    user: { login: 'github-actions[bot]', type: 'Bot' },\n    body: '<!-- calculator:coverage-gap-report -->\\n# Coverage gap report\\n...' },\n];\nconst { selected } = selectOldestOpenIssues(entries);\nconsole.log(selected.map((issue) => issue.number)); // [ 247, 254, 258 ]\nconst body = buildCombinedIssueBody({\n  repository: { owner: 'link-assistant', repo: 'calculator', fullName: 'link-assistant/calculator', url: 'https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator' },\n  issues: selected, totalOpen: entries.length, attachmentCount: selected.length,\n});\nconsole.log(body.slice(body.indexOf(REQUIRED_CLOSING_REFERENCES_HEADING)));\n// ```\n// Fixes #247\n// Fixes #254\n// Fixes #258   <- the bot-maintained status page\n// ```\n```\n\nThe full script and its output: https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/09410d73/experiments/issue-258/hive-mind-dashboard-selection-repro.mjs and https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/09410d73/docs/case-studies/issue-258/data/hive-mind-dashboard-selection-repro.txt\n\n## Root cause\n\n- [`selectOldestOpenIssues`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs#L109-L131) filters out only pull requests. It accepts an `exclude` list of issue numbers, but [`prepareRepositoryModeIssue`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.repository-mode.run.lib.mjs#L137-L141) never passes it, and no CLI option sets it.\n- Nothing looks at labels, the author type, or a body marker, so a repository cannot say \"this issue is not work\".\n- [`buildCombinedIssueBody`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.repository-mode.lib.mjs) puts every selected issue in the required closing block. Combined with the post-session link repair (#3174), the pull request ends up closing the status page whatever the agent decides.\n\n## Workarounds\n\n- In the repository: make the status workflow update its issue without reopening it, so one close sticks. Example: https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/pull/261 (`scripts/update-coverage-gap-issue.mjs` no longer sends `state`; the body lists the issues that track the actual work).\n- Close the status page as \"not planned\" before running repository mode, if its workflow does not reopen it.\n- Solve the real issues one by one (`/solve <issue-url>`) instead of using repository mode.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. **Let a repository opt issues out.** Skip open issues that carry a label from a configurable list (for example `--skip-issue-labels`, defaulting to something like `hive-mind:skip`, `dashboard`, `status`) or a body marker such as `<!-- hive-mind:skip -->`. Pass the result through the existing `exclude` option of `selectOldestOpenIssues`.\n2. **Treat bot-authored issues as opt-in, or at least flag them.** Issues with `user.type === 'Bot'` are mostly reports and dashboards (Renovate's \"Dependency Dashboard\", coverage and benchmark reports). Either skip them unless a flag includes them, or keep them but list them separately in the combined issue (\"maintained by a bot, close only if the PR changes what it reports\").\n3. **Show what was left out.** `buildCombinedIssueBody` already reports issues over the sub-issue limit. Add a line for issues skipped by label, marker or author, with the reason, so the scope stays reviewable.\n4. **Regression tests.** `selectOldestOpenIssues` with a labeled issue, a marked issue and a bot-authored issue. `prepareRepositoryModeIssue` passing the exclusions. The combined body listing the skipped issues and leaving them out of the closing block.\n\nRelated: #3174 (post-session link repair re-adds `Fixes` lines for the whole sub-issue tree).\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3176/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206","id":5842383598,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDuy7g","number":3206,"title":"Telegram bot freezes for all chats while a command prepares its task: /codex --model formal-ai blocked polling for 10 min (handlerTimeout: Infinity + awaited image pull); sync I/O audit and lint rules","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:17:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:34Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:34Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nA single `/codex … --model formal-ai` request froze the whole Telegram bot for **10 minutes** on 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8):\n\n- 21:52:05 UTC: the `/codex` handler started `docker pull ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai:0.352.1` (via `ensureFormalAiSidecarImage`, awaited inside the update handler).\n- **No `getUpdates` call between 21:51:34 and 22:02:16 UTC.** Every other user's command in every chat waited.\n- 22:02:05: the pull was killed by `DEFAULT_DOCKER_TIMEOUT_MS = 600_000` (`src/formal-ai-image.lib.mjs:65`), and the bot then fell back to the local `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8` image that was on the host all along (tracked in the pull sub-issue).\n\nRoot cause: `src/telegram-bot.mjs:212` sets `handlerTimeout: Infinity`, and Telegraf's long polling does not request the next batch until every handler of the current batch has resolved. The `/solve`/`/codex`/`/agent`/`/claude` handler `await`s `executeAndUpdateMessage(...)` (`telegram-bot.mjs:707`, `/hive` at `:883`, `/fix` in `telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs:233`, `/task` in `telegram-task-command.lib.mjs:311`), and that awaits the Formal AI image resolution, sidecar start and `$ --isolated docker` launch.\n\nInstalling or updating Formal AI (or any other slow preparation) must never block other bot operations.\n\n## Audit (main `a8bec06`, 2.35.9)\n\n**Long awaits inside update handlers** (each stalls *all* chats while it runs):\n\n| Handler | Where | Await | Typical |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| /solve, /codex, /agent, /claude, /hive, /fix, /task | `telegram-bot.mjs:707`, `:883`, `telegram-fix-command.lib.mjs:233`, `telegram-task-command.lib.mjs:311` | `executeAndUpdateMessage` → Formal AI image pull / sidecar start / container launch | seconds; **up to 10 min** on a cold Formal AI host |\n| /solve | `telegram-bot.mjs:641`, `:647`, `:666` | `validateGitHubEntityExistence`, `autoAcceptInviteForRepo`, `preflightRepositoryTarget` (sequential `gh api`) | 1–10 s |\n| /accept_invites | `telegram-accept-invitations.lib.mjs:185`, `:191` | `gh api … --paginate` | 1–30 s |\n| /merge | `telegram-merge-command.lib.mjs:329`, `:336`, `:420` | label checks, `processor.initialize()` | 1–10 s |\n\n**Synchronous I/O in the bot process** (blocks the event loop, so also polling, timers and other handlers):\n\n- `eslint-plugin-n` `n/no-sync` over `src/`: **141** calls in 25 files (many are CLI-only and fine).\n- In modules the bot loads: `bot-logger.lib.mjs` (9: `statSync` + `appendFileSync` on **every** log line, rotation with `renameSync`/`readdirSync`/`unlinkSync`), `lib.mjs:350-351` (`appendFileSync`/`chmodSync` in the stdout/stderr interceptor, on every console write), `session-store.lib.mjs` (5, `appendFileSync` per session event), `model-catalogue.lib.mjs` (4, `readFileSync` in the `/models` path), `docker-sidecar.lib.mjs` (4), `state-lock.lib.mjs` (5, a `mkdir` lock: legitimate, mark it), `isolation-runner.lib.mjs` (10), `session-resume.lib.mjs` (6), `router-session-drain.lib.mjs` (5), `agentic-cli-updater.lib.mjs` (4), `solve.disk-diagnostics.lib.mjs:50,63` (`execFileSync('du')`, reached from `session-monitor` on session completion: a `du` over a large workspace blocks the bot).\n- **60** `docker`/`git`/`gh` child processes started without a `timeout` (14 files; `github-merge.lib.mjs` 27, `github-merge-ci-signals.lib.mjs` 5, `telegram-accept-invitations.lib.mjs` 4, `solve.accept-invite.lib.mjs` 4, …).\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Handlers return immediately.** A command handler validates, replies \"Starting…\", and hands the launch to a background job (`void launch(...).catch(report)`), whose progress and errors edit that message. Image pulls, sidecar start and container launch never run on the update path.\n2. Replace `handlerTimeout: Infinity` with a finite value (Telegraf's 90 s default or less) **after** (1), so a regression shows up as a logged handler timeout instead of a frozen bot.\n3. A runtime watchdog: wrap every registered handler and log a warning (and a counter in the heartbeat) when one runs longer than 2 s. This catches transitive blocking that lint cannot see.\n4. Make the bot's hot paths async: a `fs.createWriteStream` logger (no `statSync`/`appendFileSync` per line), async session-store appends, async `du`.\n5. Lint rules, so this does not come back:\n   - `n/no-sync` (eslint-plugin-n, industry standard) as `error` for every module reachable from `src/telegram-bot.mjs` (compute the import closure in the config, rather than a filename list), with `// hive-sync-ok: <reason>` for startup-only and exit-handler code.\n   - `no-await-in-loop` (core) as `warn`.\n   - `promise/catch-or-return` (eslint-plugin-promise), so the fire-and-forget launches in (1) always handle rejection. (`@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises` needs type information; this repository is plain ESM JS.)\n   - No industry rule covers the two Hive-Mind-specific patterns, so add custom rules (drafts, tested against `main`, private gist: https://gist.github.com/konard/e621dc37520a2ab7e64a006f0832e3c7):\n     - `hive/require-exec-timeout`: every `exec`/`execFile`/`spawn` (sync or async) of `docker`, `git` or `gh` passes a `timeout` (60 findings today).\n     - `hive/no-slow-await-in-telegram-handler`: no `await` of a known-slow function (`ensureFormalAiSidecarImage`, `executeAndUpdateMessage`, `validateGitHubEntityExistence`, `sleep`, …) inside a function registered with `bot.command`/`bot.on`/`bot.hears`. The draft finds 0 today because handlers are registered by name; the rule must resolve the identifier to its declaration (scope analysis) to close that gap.\n     - `hive/no-sync-in-bot-process`: the import-closure scoping of `n/no-sync` above (27 findings with the draft's filename list).\n6. A regression test: with `docker pull` stubbed to hang, a `/codex … --model formal-ai` update must not delay the handling of a second update (e.g. `/help`) by more than 1 s.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3206/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207","id":5842383815,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDuzxw","number":3207,"title":"Formal AI sidecar image: pulls 6.2 GB from ghcr before using the local Hive Mind image with the same version, 600 s timeout reported as 'unknown', cancelled pull leaks ~17.7 GB for 6 h","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:17:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:35Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nOn 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8, host with Docker 29.6.1 / containerd image store), the first `--model formal-ai` task on the host (`/codex …`, session `67c6a8b5-28ce-48f7-ba89-8e33278f2749`, execution `4d45ad2c-90e8-45b7-92eb-1c63aa270972`) spent **10 minutes** pulling an image it did not need, and the cancelled pull leaked **~17.7 GB** of disk for 6 hours:\n\n1. `resolveFormalAiSidecarImageCandidates` (`src/formal-ai-image.lib.mjs:205`) tries `ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai:0.352.1` (6.20 GB compressed, 24.3 GB on disk) **before** the local `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8`, which already bakes the same Formal AI 0.352.1 and was on the host.\n2. `docker pull` ran 21:52:05 → 22:02:05 UTC and was killed by `DEFAULT_DOCKER_TIMEOUT_MS = 600_000` (`:65`). A killed `execFile` has empty stderr, so `classifyDockerRegistryError` returned `kind: 'unknown'`, \"the pull failed\" — the log does not say it timed out.\n3. Then the local image was used, and the sidecar was healthy in seconds:\n   `[VERBOSE] formal-ai-image: using 'konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8' (hive-mind-image) already present locally`.\n4. The cancelled pull left 49 Formal-AI-only content blobs (6.20 GB) and 30 unpacked snapshots referenced by no image or container (11.90 GiB), held by containerd lease `670759184-l9sp` with `containerd.io/gc.expire` 6 h after the pull (dockerd: `Cancel with lease, leased resources will remain until expiration`, `failed to cleanup extract-… NotFound`). On this host that was 63 GB used instead of ~45 GB until the lease expired.\n5. All of it ran inside the Telegram update handler, freezing the bot (separate sub-issue).\n\n## Expected\n\n- **Prefer what is already on the host**: if a local image provides the required Formal AI version (the Hive Mind image bakes it; its version is known), use it first; pull only when no local image qualifies.\n- **Pull the slim image** (`ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai:<v>-slim`, 0.33 GB compressed for 0.353.2) for the sidecar, which only runs `formal-ai serve` (link-assistant/formal-ai#1153).\n- Pull in the background with progress, never on the request path; a timeout is reported as `kind: 'timeout'` (\"did not finish in 10 min\"), with the bytes done.\n- After a cancelled/timed-out pull, release what it left: `docker image prune` does not reach lease-held content, so either avoid the cancel (let the background pull finish) or report the leaked size and the lease expiry in the log, and let the disk-cleanup path account for it.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3207/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208","id":5842384033,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu0oQ","number":3208,"title":"Formal AI updater accepts an image no task used, unload deletes it 5 h later, and the next task must re-pull 7 GB or fail closed although no memory was migrated","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:17:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:35Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nThe Formal AI updater, the 5-hour unload and the fail-closed rule combine so that the *next* Formal AI task on a host depends on re-downloading a 7 GB image within 10 minutes, for an update that was never used:\n\nState on the host now (`~/.hive-mind/state/formal-ai-sidecar.json`, read 2026-10-14 05:20 UTC):\n\n```json\n\"lastUpdate\": { \"image\": \"ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai:latest\", \"digest\": \"sha256:01da160c…\", \"version\": \"0.353.2\",\n                \"migrationId\": null, \"memorySchemaVersion\": null, \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-13T23:22:54.764Z\" },\n\"serving\":    { \"image\": \"konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8\", \"version\": \"0.352.1\", \"memorySchemaVersion\": null, \"observedAt\": \"2026-10-13T22:10:58.172Z\" },\n\"lastUsedAt\": \"2026-10-13T23:09:05.730Z\",\n\"lastUnload\": { \"at\": \"2026-10-14T04:10:20.038Z\", \"images\": [\"sha256:01da160c…\"], \"bytesFreed\": 28970000000 }\n```\n\nTimeline (UTC): tasks ran Formal AI **0.352.1** (from the Hive Mind image) at 22:02–22:18 → the updater pulled and **accepted** `formal-ai:latest` = **0.353.2** at 23:22 (the 0.353.x tags have no GitHub Release yet: link-assistant/formal-ai#1203) → no task used it → the unload removed it at 04:10 (\"Formal AI unloaded (unused for 5h1s): removed 1 image… freeing 28.97GB\").\n\nConsequences:\n\n1. `resolveAcceptedFormalAiImageCandidates` (`src/formal-ai-image.lib.mjs:170`) now returns only the accepted 0.353.2 candidates (not local, so it pulls the repo digest / `:0.353.2` / `:latest`, 7.12 GB compressed) under the same 600 s timeout. If that pull fails, the task fails closed: \"Hive Mind will not fall back to an older Formal AI release against memory an accepted update already migrated.\"\n2. But nothing was migrated: `migrationId: null`, `memorySchemaVersion: null`, and the sidecar health check logged `memory schema=unknown` for the image that actually served. The fail-closed rule (issue #2207) is applied without the condition it exists for.\n3. The updater pulls and accepts updates for a host where Formal AI is idle and about to be unloaded, then the unload deletes the update: 7 GB downloaded and 29 GB unpacked for nothing, every release.\n4. `formal-ai-unload: no Formal AI image on this host` is logged while `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8` (which serves Formal AI) is present, and `bytesFreed` reports the uncompressed size, not the disk actually freed (shared layers).\n\n## Expected\n\n- Fail closed only when the accepted update really migrated memory (`migrationId`/`memorySchemaVersion` set). Otherwise fall back to the newest locally available image, with a visible warning.\n- The updater does not pull for an idle host (or pulls the slim image), and an update is \"accepted\" only once a task has run on it; or the unload keeps the accepted image's identity so the next task pulls in the background before the task needs it.\n- The sidecar health reports a real `memory.schema_version` (Formal AI side, if missing) so the state is not `unknown`.\n- The unload log and `bytesFreed` describe the real effect.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3208/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209","id":5842384240,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu1cA","number":3209,"title":"Docker session reported '✅ finished successfully' after 11 s before its container existed (exitCode null → 0); the real failure 26 min later was never reported (#2189 latch)","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:18:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:36Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:36Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nA Docker-isolated session was reported **finished successfully after 11 s, before its container existed**, and its real failure 26 minutes later was never reported.\n\n`/codex https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/issues/1 --model formal-ai` on 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8), session `67c6a8b5-28ce-48f7-ba89-8e33278f2749`, execution `4d45ad2c-90e8-45b7-92eb-1c63aa270972`:\n\n| UTC | Bot log |\n|---|---|\n| 21:52:05 | session tracked; Formal AI image pull starts (the container is created only after the sidecar is ready) |\n| 21:52:15 | `isolation-runner: Status query result: ` (empty) · `docker inspect … not running` · **\"Session … has finished\"** |\n| 21:52:16 | Telegram: **\"✅ Work session finished successfully, ⏱️ Duration: 11s\"** · `session_completion_notified {\"exitCode\":null}` · `removed from tracking (exit: 0)` |\n| 22:02:12 | the container is actually started |\n| 22:02:44 | \"Session … was already reported at 21:52:16; finalizing without repeating the completion work (issue #2189)\" — dropped again |\n| 22:18:13 | the run fails (exit 1, `❌ AI session failed (tool_failure)`) — **no Telegram update**; the message still says ✅ |\n\nCode: the status poll (`session-monitor.isolation-state.lib.mjs`, fallback to `runner.isSessionRunning` when `$ --status` has no record yet) treats \"no container yet\" as \"not running\", and `completionExitForAudit` turns `exitCode: null` into `0` (`session-monitor.lib.mjs`). The #2189 completion latch then makes the false completion permanent.\n\n## Expected\n\n- A session is not finished until its container (or `$` execution) has been seen at least once, or the launch itself has failed: keep a `launched`/`containerSeen` state, like the sidecar lease already does.\n- `exitCode: null` is never reported as success. Unknown → \"status unknown\", not ✅.\n- If a session that was marked complete is later found running, un-latch it (or never latch a completion that had `exitCode: null`), so the real end is reported.\n- Regression test: a launch that takes longer than one poll interval (e.g. a slow image pull) is reported only when the container exits, with its real exit code.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3209/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210","id":5842384459,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu2Sw","number":3210,"title":"Formal AI sidecar lease kept for 1 h after its task container exited: containerSeen is set only when the container is seen running","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:18:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:37Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:37Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\n`reconcileSidecarLeases` (`src/docker-sidecar.lib.mjs`, used for the Formal AI sidecar) sets `containerSeen` only when it observes the task container **running**. A container that started and exited between two reconcile ticks is `exists=true running=false` with `containerSeen=false`, so the lease is kept for the whole `LEASE_START_GRACE_MS = 60 * 60 * 1000` launch grace:\n\n```\n[VERBOSE] formal-ai-sidecar: keeping lease '435374e0-3e09-4e3d-9b8e-05f63a29093d' whose container has not appeared yet (…s into the 3600s launch grace)\n… (repeated for ~1 hour) …\n[VERBOSE] formal-ai-sidecar: dropping stale lease '435374e0-3e09-4e3d-9b8e-05f63a29093d' (container exists=true running=false)\n```\n\nObserved on 2026-10-13 (2.35.8) for the `/agent … --model formal-ai` run (session `435374e0-3e09-4e3d-9b8e-05f63a29093d`, execution `05c82f00-9417-4ebb-8c8c-97f2b893dd00`, ran 22:05:49–22:07:37 UTC), and for `67c6a8b5-28ce-48f7-ba89-8e33278f2749`. The message is also wrong: the container *had* appeared. The stale lease keeps the sidecar (and its memory) up for an hour and delays the idle clock.\n\n## Expected\n\n- `containerSeen = true` whenever the container **exists** (running or exited); an existing, stopped container ends the lease at once.\n- The launch grace applies only while the container does not exist, and should be tied to the launch state (pulling/starting) rather than a fixed hour.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3210/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211","id":5842384687,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu3Lw","number":3211,"title":"No-progress sessions reported as success: /claude --model formal-ai (2 turns, no commit) marked PR ready + 🎉 SUCCESS; /codex 73 identical calls → '✅ Codex command completed'","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:18:04Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:37Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:37Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nTwo Formal AI sessions that produced nothing were reported as successful work (2026-10-13, Hive Mind 2.35.8).\n\n### `/claude` — \"✅ Work session finished successfully\", PR marked ready\n\n`/claude https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-fa49-7c9d-a664-b7ea33bb698a/issues/1 --model formal-ai`, session `e5faacab-558b-4c7d-b50c-73c4dfd61851`, execution `ee51df2f-6515-4273-bb9d-1785f662fbe4` (log, private gist: https://gist.github.com/konard/150f5af4368249c49b6d20dad9f69fcf):\n\n- `📊 Session num_turns: 2`: one `WebFetch`, then a final text that only restated the tool output (Formal AI side: link-assistant/formal-ai#1206). No `Write`/`Edit`/`Bash`, **no commit in this session**.\n- Hive Mind still logged `📝 Converting PR: To ready for review (solution draft verified)…`, `🎉 SUCCESS: A solution draft has been prepared as a pull request`, and Telegram showed ✅ (4m 19s).\n- Why the guard passed: `ensurePullRequestIsReady({ requireChanges: true })` (`src/solve.results.lib.mjs:802`, issue #2247) measures the **PR's** diff against its base. PR #2 already had 7 commits from earlier sessions, so the diff was non-empty although this session changed nothing. The \"⚠️ No progress: this session ended exactly like the previous one\" check exists, but only in the auto-restart path. `solve.mjs:1279` also calls `ensurePullRequestIsReady` without `requireChanges`.\n- An earlier Formal AI session's working-session summary on the same PR is \"The `pwd` command completed. Output: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-…\": the model's last echo, posted as the summary.\n\n### `/codex` — 73 identical calls, then \"✅ Codex command completed\"\n\n`/codex https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/issues/1 --model formal-ai`, session `67c6a8b5-28ce-48f7-ba89-8e33278f2749`, execution `4d45ad2c-90e8-45b7-92eb-1c63aa270972` (log: https://gist.github.com/konard/b5819c8d2e68268c18f34ba97f0b7601):\n\n- The same `gh issue view '…/issues/1' --json title --jq .title` ran **73 times** (≈14 min, **6,121,680 input tokens**), Formal AI side: link-assistant/formal-ai#1154.\n- solve logged `✅ Codex command completed`, and only the later auto-restart noticed \"No progress\".\n\nPer #2395 the repeated-tool-call breaker stays **off** by default: legitimate polling must never be interrupted. This issue is about the **reported outcome**, not about killing sessions.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Success requires progress **by this session**: compare the branch head (and working tree) at session start and end. No new commit/change → \"⚠️ finished without changes\" (Telegram and PR comment), PR not converted to ready, never 🎉 SUCCESS. Apply it to every tool (claude, codex, agent, …), not only the auto-restart path.\n- A session whose tool calls are dominated by one identical call (e.g. ≥10 identical non-polling calls with identical output) is reported as \"looped on `<command>` N times\", using the existing breaker's detector in observe-only mode, without stopping the session.\n- The working-session summary is not a raw echo of the model's last tool output.\n- Regression tests with recorded Formal AI transcripts of both runs.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3211/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212","id":5842384899,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu4Aw","number":3212,"title":"Codex auto-restart iteration of a --model formal-ai run lost the Formal AI provider and called ChatGPT (400 model not supported), then reported 'Authentication error'","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:18:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:38Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:38Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nIn the `--auto-restart-until-mergeable` iteration of a `--model formal-ai` codex run, Codex was started **without the Formal AI provider** and called ChatGPT. Then the failure was reported with the wrong reason.\n\n`/codex https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/issues/1 --model formal-ai` (2026-10-13, Hive Mind 2.35.8), execution `4d45ad2c-90e8-45b7-92eb-1c63aa270972`, log (private gist): https://gist.github.com/konard/b5819c8d2e68268c18f34ba97f0b7601\n\n| | First iteration | Restart iteration 1/5 (22:17 UTC) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `🧠 Formal AI: local wrapper / serving backend / protocol / config CODEX_HOME=…/formal-ai/codex-…` | present | **absent** |\n| `🧭 Formal AI pinned to verified Codex capability state: …/repositories/konard/test-hello-world-…` | present | **absent** |\n| Capability preflight on the repository-scoped `CODEX_HOME` | yes | yes (re-run, rewrites that home) |\n| Codex result | talked to Formal AI | `turn.failed` **400 \"The 'formal-ai' model is not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account.\"** |\n\nThe printed command is identical in both iterations (`export FORMAL_AI_API_KEY=[REDACTED]; export CODEX_HOME=/home/box/.codex/hive-mind/repositories/…; codex exec --model \"formal-ai\" …`), so the difference is the `config.toml` in that home: the restart's capability preflight wrote a fresh one, and the Formal AI provider block that `executeCodex` copies in (`src/codex.lib.mjs` ~661-680) was not copied again because `resolveFormalAiToolExecution` did not run/log in the restart path (`solve.keep-working.lib.mjs` → `solve.restart-shared.lib.mjs` → `executeCodex`). Exact cause still to be confirmed with verbose logging in that path.\n\nThen the outcome was misreported:\n\n- PR comment: \"🚨 Solution Draft Failed … Reason: **Authentication error**\".\n- `ℹ️ PR #2 stays a draft: Model metadata for \\`formal-ai\\` not found. Defaulting to fallback metadata…` — a non-fatal Codex warning shown as the failure cause.\n- The real cause (the provider was not Formal AI; ChatGPT rejected the model) appears nowhere in the summary.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Every iteration (first, auto-restart, auto-continue, resume) of a Formal AI run goes through the same Formal AI wiring and logs the `🧠 Formal AI:` lines; a test asserts that the restart's `CODEX_HOME/config.toml` names the Formal AI provider.\n- If the wiring cannot be applied, fail with \"Formal AI provider not configured\" before starting Codex. Never let a Formal AI run reach a vendor endpoint (#2146 fail-closed).\n- `turn.failed` 400 \"model is not supported\" is classified as a configuration error, not \"Authentication error\", and the \"Model metadata … not found\" warning is never reported as the failure reason.\n- Codex shows \"Model metadata for `formal-ai` not found\" on every turn: register model metadata for `formal-ai` in the generated config (context window etc.) so Codex has none of these fallbacks, as for OpenAI models.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3212/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213","id":5842385131,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu46w","number":3213,"title":"/agent run fails on any recoverable tool error: a failed read ('e.g', File not found) is treated as a fatal error event","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:18:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:39Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:39Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\n`/agent https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/issues/1 --model formal-ai` (2026-10-13, Hive Mind 2.35.8, agent 0.26.13), session `435374e0-3e09-4e3d-9b8e-05f63a29093d`, execution `05c82f00-9417-4ebb-8c8c-97f2b893dd00`, log (private gist): https://gist.github.com/konard/a26a79ab44357a50859a51ff7f762af6\n\n- Formal AI's first tool call was `read` on `…/e.g` (link-assistant/formal-ai#1189) → `File not found`, an ordinary tool result.\n- `@link-assistant/agent` emits a top-level `{\"type\":\"error\"}` for every failed tool call (link-assistant/agent#332).\n- Hive Mind's streaming detection (`src/agent.lib.mjs` ~827, issue #1201) and `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery` (`src/agent-command.lib.mjs` ~107-120) treat it as fatal: \"Agent exited 0 after an error event; the error event in its output still fails the run\".\n- Reported: `❌ AGENT execution failed with Agent reported error: Error: File not found: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791929210941/e.g` — the reason shown is a tool error, not why the session really failed (Formal AI stopped and asked \"Reply `Report issue`\", link-assistant/formal-ai#1205).\n\nAny recoverable tool error fails an `/agent` run, with every model.\n\n## Expected\n\n- An error event whose payload is a tool part (`part.type === \"tool\"`, or the `recoverable`/`tool_error` marker that link-assistant/agent#332 adds) is not fatal; only session-level errors are.\n- Success/failure of an agent run follows the session result (exit code, final message, progress made), and the failure reason names the last fatal event.\n- Test with a recorded stream: a failed `read` followed by a successful turn is a success.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3213/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214","id":5842385349,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXDu5xQ","number":3214,"title":"In-place resume from a committed dind container: nested dockerd refuses to start ('delete /var/run/docker.pid: process with PID 25 is still running')","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:18:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:40Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nWhen a Docker-isolated task is resumed in place from its committed container (kill / OOM recovery), the nested Docker daemon cannot start:\n\n```\nfailed to start daemon … delete /var/run/docker.pid: process with PID 25 is still running\n```\n\nObserved on 2026-10-13 (Hive Mind 2.35.8, start-command 0.37.1, task image `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.35.8` = `ghcr.io/link-foundation/box-dind:2.10.4` base) for `Godmy/stylist-svelte#5`, execution `1a664acf-1a63-4973-a4a7-32fc9088c98e`, container `d5173fa1-9c62-4b9b-979f-5748624f3860`: the first attempt was killed by the cgroup OOM killer (3 GB limit), and the in-place resume started from the committed filesystem, which still contains `/var/run/docker.pid` (and possibly `containerd.pid`) from the dead container. In the new container PID 25 is some other process, so dockerd refuses to start. (That resume then also exited 127 on `/claude`, see #2630 / #2887.)\n\n## Expected\n\n- Before the resumed container starts dockerd, remove stale pid files (`/var/run/docker.pid`, `/var/run/docker/containerd/containerd.pid`, `/var/run/containerd/containerd.pid`) when the PID does not belong to a running dockerd/containerd. A `RUN rm` in `Dockerfile.dind` is not enough: the file comes from the committed snapshot, so do it in the resume entrypoint/handoff script, or exclude `/var/run` from the commit.\n- If the box-dind entrypoint is the right place, report it to link-foundation/box as well.\n- Test: commit a container with a running dind, start a new container from it, dockerd starts.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3214/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630","id":5747949853,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABVprBHQ","number":2630,"title":"Session-kill recovery runs the Telegram alias as a command ('sh: /claude: not found', exit 127): killed task never resumed, 4.4 GB resume snapshot leaked","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-07T15:59:46Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:40Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":29937030,"node_id":"IT_kwDODp_H0c4ByM2G","name":"Bug","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","color":"red","created_at":"2025-11-21T09:35:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T09:35:16Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nAn automatic session-kill recovery ran the **Telegram command alias** as a shell command inside the resumed container, so the recovery died immediately:\n\n```\n$ docker logs e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b-resume-1\n[dind-entrypoint] Starting dockerd (storage-driver=fuse-overlayfs, data-root=/var/lib/docker)\n[dind-entrypoint] dockerd is ready after 1s\n[dind-entrypoint] image preload/passthrough complete\nsh: 1: /claude: not found                                  # exit 127\n```\n\n```\n$ docker inspect -f '{{json .Config.Cmd}}' e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b-resume-1\n[\"sh\",\"-c\",\"/claude https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 --think high --tool claude --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en --resume 41cebf9b-7516-44c0-8422-5bbafe26cee9\"]\n```\n\nSide effects:\n- The killed task (link-assistant/hive-mind#2591 / PR #2592) was **never resumed**. Its work survives only on `recovery/issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2`.\n- start-command's in-place resume ran `docker commit` on the stopped container, which left an image `start-command-resume/e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b:1` with **4.43 GB unique size**. It also left a stopped container `…-resume-1`. `hive-cleanup` sees neither (see #2629).\n\n## Timeline (UTC, 2026-10-07; hive-mind 2.33.11, start-command 0.35.1)\n\n| Time | Event |\n|---|---|\n| 09:07:42 | Task started from Telegram `/claude https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 --think high` in container `e6c1dd3f-…` (`d9a38c244727`), memory limit 2.92 GiB |\n| ~09:40 | `claude` killed: `CLAUDE execution failed with Claude command failed with exit code 137`; Docker `OOMKilled=true`. Failure comment: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2592#issuecomment-6035301295 (also referenced in #2613) |\n| 09:42:47 | Container exits 1. Uncommitted work is pushed to `recovery/issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2` |\n| 09:54:08 | Session-kill recovery: `$ --resume e6c1dd3f-… -- \"/claude … --resume 41cebf9b-…\"` → `docker commit` → container `e6c1dd3f-…-resume-1` |\n| 09:54:13 | `sh: 1: /claude: not found`, exit 127. No further attempt |\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/session-resume.lib.mjs` → `buildResumeCommand()` (same on `main`, line 264):\n\n```js\nconst commandAlias = typeof sessionInfo.commandAlias === 'string' && /^[a-z0-9_-]+$/i.test(sessionInfo.commandAlias) ? sessionInfo.commandAlias : null;\nconst bin = binary || (commandAlias ? `/${commandAlias}` : command);\n...\nreturn { binary: bin, args, display: `${bin} ${args.map(quoteArg).join(' ')}` };\n```\n\n`/${commandAlias}` is a *Telegram* command (`/claude`, `/codex`, ...), meant only for the \"♻️ Resume from last session\" chat message. But `src/session-kill-resume.in-place.lib.mjs` (line 197 on `main`) executes that display string:\n\n```js\nconst result = await runner.resumeIsolatedSession(decision.identifier, { command: plan?.command?.display || null, verbose });\n```\n\nSo every in-place recovery of a task started through a Telegram alias (`/claude`, `/codex`, `/agent`, ...) is broken, while tasks started with `/solve` work.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. Keep two fields in `buildResumeCommand()`. One is the executable command: `binary` = `solve` (or the persisted real command), with the args. The other is the chat text: `chatDisplay` = `/${commandAlias} …`. Pass only the executable one to `resumeIsolatedSession()`. The alias's implied options are already in `sessionInfo.args` (`--tool claude` is present above).\n2. Before calling `$ --resume … -- <command>`, assert that the first word of the command resolves inside the image (`command -v solve`), or use the absolute `exec 'solve' …` form that the original start command uses.\n3. Treat a recovery that exits **127 or 126 within seconds** as a failed recovery. Report it on the PR/issue and in Telegram (\"automatic recovery could not start: …\") instead of silently stopping. Retry with the fresh-launch path (`executeWithIsolation`) that `session-kill-resume.lib.mjs` already has.\n4. When a snapshot resume fails, remove the derived `-resume-N` container and its `start-command-resume/<uuid>:<n>` image, or at least report them. Otherwise each failed recovery leaks a full writable-layer copy (4.4 GB here).\n\n## Tests to add\n\n- `buildResumeCommand({ sessionInfo: { command: 'solve', commandAlias: 'claude', args: [url, '--tool', 'claude'] }, lastSessionId })`: the executable command must start with `solve` and the display may start with `/claude`.\n- An in-place resume plan built for an alias-launched session must not contain a leading `/` word in the command passed to `resumeIsolatedSession`.\n\n## Workaround\n\nResume manually: `$ --resume e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b -- \"solve https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 --think high --tool claude --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en --resume 41cebf9b-7516-44c0-8422-5bbafe26cee9\"`, or continue from branch `recovery/issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2`.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/332","id":5842317139,"node_id":"I_kwDOQYTy3M8AAAABXDqvUw","number":332,"title":"A recoverable failed tool call is emitted as a fatal top-level {\"type\":\"error\"} event, so Hive Mind fails the whole run","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T05:10:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T06:57:26Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T06:57:26Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem\n\nA tool call that fails and is *recovered from* is emitted as a top-level `{\"type\":\"error\"}` event, the same event type used for fatal session errors. Consumers cannot tell \"the model asked for a missing file and got an error result\" from \"the session failed\".\n\n`js/src/cli/event-handler.js` (main, 1197d6c):\n\n```js\nif (part.type === 'tool') {\n  eventHandler.output({ type: 'tool_use', ..., part });\n  // If tool failed, also output an error event\n  if (part.state?.status === 'error') {\n    eventHandler.output({ type: 'error', ..., part, message: errorText(stateError, 'Tool execution failed'), error: stateError || 'Tool execution failed' });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `tool_use` event already carries `part.state.status === \"error\"` and the error text, so the extra top-level event only duplicates it, under the fatal type.\n\n## Impact (observed 2026-10-13, agent 0.26.13, Hive Mind 2.35.8)\n\n`/agent https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/issues/1 --model formal-ai`, execution `05c82f00-9417-4ebb-8c8c-97f2b893dd00`:\n\n- The model called `read` on `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-…/e.g` (formal-ai bug link-assistant/formal-ai#1189). The tool returned `File not found`, which is a normal, recoverable tool result.\n- agent emitted a top-level `type:\"error\"` event for it.\n- Hive Mind (`src/agent.lib.mjs` streaming detection, `src/agent-command.lib.mjs` `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery`, issue link-assistant/hive-mind#1201 logic) treats any top-level error event as fatal: *\"Agent exited 0 after an error event; the error event in its output still fails the run\"*. The run failed with `❌ AGENT execution failed with Agent reported error: Error: File not found: …/e.g`.\n\nThis affects every model, not only Formal AI: any recoverable tool error (a missing file, a non-zero `bash` exit with `--fail` semantics, a bad edit anchor) fails the whole Hive Mind run, and the reported reason names the tool error instead of the real outcome.\n\nLog (private gist, sanitized): https://gist.github.com/konard/a26a79ab44357a50859a51ff7f762af6\n\n## Expected\n\n- A failed tool call is reported only on its `tool_use` event (`part.state.status: \"error\"`), or, if a separate event is kept, with a distinct type such as `tool_error`, or `type:\"error\"` with `\"recoverable\": true` / `\"scope\": \"tool\"`.\n- `type:\"error\"` without a recoverable flag is reserved for errors that end the session or turn.\n- Document the contract in the JSON event docs so consumers (Hive Mind) can rely on it, and add a test: a session in which a tool fails and the model continues must not contain a fatal `error` event.\n\nHive Mind side: link-assistant/hive-mind#3213 (umbrella link-assistant/hive-mind#3215).\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248","id":5844603295,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXF2Rnw","number":3248,"title":"Formal AI Draft workflow fails on every new issue (53/60 runs since 2026-10-07): a failed 'e.g' read fails the run; no-op drafts; false 'log not attached'; Formal AI cache pushed as recovery branches","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:34:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:41Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\n`Formal AI Draft` (`.github/workflows/formal-ai-draft.yml`, triggered by `issues: opened`) **failed on 53 of the last 60 issue-triggered runs** (2026-10-07 → 2026-10-14). The other 7 runs were skipped by the `no-formal-ai-draft` label. No issue got a usable draft.\n\n| Cause | Runs |\n|---|---|\n| `❌ Agent reported error: Error: File not found: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-…/e.g` | **51** |\n| `docker run` exit 125: Docker Hub auth timeout while pulling `konard/hive-mind:latest` ([37993992264](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/37993992264), [37993481615](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/37993481615)) | 2 |\n\nLatest run: [38515996193](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/38515996193) (issue #3215, draft PR #3225, solve v2.35.9, formal-ai 0.353.1). First run in the sample: [37691785246](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/37691785246).\n\n## Root cause (verified in the run logs)\n\nThe failure is a chain of three defects. Each one alone would turn a failed tool call into a failed run:\n\n1. **Formal AI** treats the abbreviation in \"(e.g., returns empty content…)\" in Hive Mind's system prompt as a file. Its first action in every run is `Let me open e.g and read what it says.`, then `read /tmp/gh-issue-solver-…/e.g` → `File not found`. Temperature is 0, so this is deterministic. → link-assistant/formal-ai#1189\n2. **agent** emits that recoverable tool failure as a top-level `{\"type\":\"error\"}` event. → link-assistant/agent#332, **fixed in agent 0.26.14** (released 2026-10-14 07:01Z; verified below).\n3. **solve** fails the run on any error record in the output, even when the agent continued, completed and exited 0:\n   - log line: `ℹ️ Agent exited 0 after an error event; the error event in its output still fails the run`\n   - code: `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery` in `src/agent-command.lib.mjs:116-122`, by design since #1201\n   - → #3213\n\nHow it played out by version:\n- **0.352.1 (41 runs):** Formal AI stopped right after the error and asked `Reply \\`Report issue\\`` (formal-ai#1205).\n- **0.353.1 (10 runs):** Formal AI recovered and kept working (gh issue view, webfetch, bash), and solve then failed the run anyway because of step 3.\n\n**Even with all three fixed, the draft would still produce nothing.** Formal AI 0.353.1 ends with `terminal_state \"planned_not_executed\"`, and its goal is Hive Mind's entire prompt rather than the issue (link-assistant/formal-ai#1209, a regression of formal-ai#1064). Hive Mind would then report the run as a success with no change made (#3211).\n\n## Live re-check: run [38536131210](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/38536131210) (this issue, PR #3249, 2026-10-14 08:35Z)\n\nAt start, the runtime updater moved agent from 0.26.13 to 0.26.14 (`agentic-cli-updater: 1 updated`). The `e.g` read failed again, but it was **no longer a fatal error event**, and the session went on. It then hit the next blockers:\n\n- **Formal AI 0.353.1 created garbage files.** It wrote `e.g` and `formal-ai-draft.yml` into the repo root, filled with the fetched GitHub page text, and said \"Created and verified\" (link-assistant/formal-ai#1211).\n- **Restart loop.** The untracked `e.g`, `formal-ai-draft.yml` and `data/cache/` (formal-ai#1208) triggered **`--auto-restart-on-uncommitted-changes` 5 of 5 times**:\n  - 18 PR comments, 7 `Add development log` commits, 28 min (08:37 → 09:05);\n  - then `❌ Auto-restart limit reached` and another `recovery/issue-3248-…` branch.\n- **Broken command on every restart.** Each restart ran `gh pr view … --comments --json comments,reviews`, which gh rejects (exit 1), then stopped (formal-ai#1158 comment).\n- **The log link works on this path.** The comment `📎 Log file uploaded as Repository` links the committed `solve.log`. Only the failure-comment path (item 3) is wrong.\n\n## Proposed fixes in Hive Mind\n\n1. **Tool errors are not run errors (#3213).** In `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery` and the output error detection, classify an error record whose part is a tool call (`part.type === 'tool'` with `part.state.status === 'error'`) as recoverable. Fail only on session or provider errors that no later completion follows, or on a non-zero exit. Add a test from run 38515996193's stream: `read e.g` fails, the session continues, exit 0 → not failed on that error.\n2. **A draft that changes nothing is a failure, with the reason given (#3211).** After the session, if the branch has no commits beyond `Initial commit with task details` and the development log, end with \"Formal AI produced no change\" plus Formal AI's terminal state (for example `planned_not_executed`). It must not be \"success\", and not the unrelated first tool error either.\n3. **The failure comment must point to the log that exists.**\n   - **What happened:**\n     - The PR #3225 comment (05:31:44Z) says `⚠️ Log Upload Failed … not attached here` (`gh-upload-log`: HTTP 403, a workflow `GITHUB_TOKEN` cannot create gists).\n     - It points to `/home/box/logs/solve-….log` inside a `docker run --rm` container that no longer exists.\n     - Yet two seconds later (05:31:46Z) `--development-log` committed the **complete** log: `dev/log/issues/3215/pulls/3225/sessions/…/solve.log`, 1,095,066 bytes.\n     - The workflow artifact `formal-ai-draft-session-3215` was uploaded too.\n   - **Fix:**\n     - Commit the development log before writing the comment, and link that file.\n     - When running in Actions, also link the run's artifact (`$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID`).\n     - Never print a container path for a `--rm` container.\n   - **Code:** `src/log-upload-failure.lib.mjs:84`, `src/log-upload.lib.mjs:373`.\n4. **Don't preserve Formal AI's own state as user work.**\n   - **What happened:** on 0.353.1, Formal AI writes `data/cache/derivations/answer_*.lino` into the workspace (link-assistant/formal-ai#1208). `commitUncommittedChangesOnCriticalError` (`src/critical-error-commit.lib.mjs`) then pushed them as **10 branches** `recovery/issue-3206-…` to `recovery/issue-3215-…`, which hold nothing else.\n   - **Fix:**\n     - Start the task-owned `formal-ai serve` with a cwd outside the repository and with `FORMAL_AI_CACHE_DIR` set to the session's own cache.\n     - Skip `data/cache/derivations/` and `.formal-ai/` in the preservation step, the same way build output is skipped already.\n     - Delete the 10 junk recovery branches once confirmed.\n5. **Pull the image with retries, and pin it.**\n   - Pull before `docker run` with retries and backoff, since 2 runs died on a single registry timeout.\n   - Use the image of the version in the checked-out `package.json` instead of `:latest`. Then the workflow scripts and the image always match, and a run is reproducible.\n   - The pull takes ~5 min of each run (05:22:42Z → 05:27:33Z in 38515996193).\n6. **Make the draft's checks visible on the PR.** PR #3225 shows only CodeQL:\n   - its `pull_request` runs (Checks and release, Security) wait in `action_required`;\n   - the dispatched runs (e.g. [38517135151](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/38517135151), success) are not attached to the PR.\n   - Fix: post the dispatched results as commit statuses on the head SHA, or as a summary comment.\n7. **Turn off the uncommitted-changes restart for drafts.** `DRAFT_SOLVE_FLAGS` (`scripts/formal-ai-draft.lib.mjs:86`) turns off `--auto-restart-until-mergeable` to keep one attempt per run. It leaves `--auto-restart-on-uncommitted-changes` on (default true, `src/solve.config.lib.mjs:244`), so the \"solve's own restart loop is disabled\" comment in `formal-ai-draft.yml` is not true.\n   - Add `--no-auto-restart-on-uncommitted-changes` and cover it in `tests/formal-ai-draft-2233.test.mjs`.\n   - In general (Telegram too), files the tool itself writes for its own state (`data/cache/derivations/`, `.formal-ai/`) should not count as \"uncommitted changes\" that restart the model.\n8. **Reuse:** add `workflow_call` to `formal-ai-draft.yml`, with inputs for the image and the Formal AI binary source, so link-assistant/formal-ai can run the same workflow on its own issues (link-assistant/formal-ai#1210).\n\n## Backlog the failing runs left\n\nOpen now in this repository:\n- **15** open draft `[WIP]` PRs by `app/github-actions` from these drafts (45 open PRs by that author in total);\n- **11** `recovery/*` branches, 10 of them from the 2026-10-14 drafts;\n- for scale: 1406 `issue-*` branches from all solve runs, not only drafts.\n\nThe daily `health` job reports attempts, but nothing flags that 100% of them fail for one known reason.\n\nSuggestion: the health job fails when the same `decision_code` or first error repeats N times in a row, and names the tracking issue.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA newly opened issue in this repository gets a draft run where:\n- a failed tool call does not end the run;\n- a run that changes nothing is reported as failed, with Formal AI's terminal state as the reason;\n- the failure comment links the complete log (committed file and/or artifact);\n- no `recovery/*` branch holds Formal AI cache files;\n- an image pull failure is retried.\n\nParent: #3215. Related: #2233, #1201, #3211, #3213, link-assistant/agent#332, link-assistant/formal-ai#1189, #1205, #1208, #1209, #1210, #1211, #1158.\n","closed_by":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277","id":5852728229,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNmLpQ","number":3277,"title":"Live verification of #3215 after deploying 2.35.10: Formal AI Hello World through /claude, /codex and /agent on a host with no cached image","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:47:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Why\n\n#3225 merged the Hive Mind side of #3215 and was released as 2.35.10, but its description says: \"**No live end-to-end run.** The issue's 'Done when' … was not run from this PR.\" So #3215 is not delivered until this run passes. This issue tracks that run and nothing else.\n\n## State on 2026-10-15\n\n- Production host: hive-mind **2.35.8** and agent **0.26.14** (read with `hive --version` / `agent --version` in the `hive-mind` container). 2.35.10, with agent pinned to 0.26.15, is not deployed yet. The maintainer deploys it with their own deploy script, never from a session.\n- Formal AI: the latest is 0.353.2 on crates.io and ghcr (`-slim` 328 MB compressed), but the latest GitHub Release is still v0.352.1 (link-assistant/formal-ai#1203).\n- The Formal AI blockers for a correct program are still open: link-assistant/formal-ai#1189, link-assistant/formal-ai#1205, link-assistant/formal-ai#1206, link-assistant/formal-ai#1209, link-assistant/formal-ai#1211, umbrella link-assistant/formal-ai#1207. So a run is **expected to fail**. This issue still needs it, because the failure has to be clean and complete:\n\n## Done when (per client: `/claude`, `/codex`, `/agent`, each with `--model formal-ai`)\n\n1. On a fresh Hello World repository, on a host whose Formal AI image was removed first:\n   - the image is pulled in the background, and the bot stays responsive while it pulls (#3206);\n   - the session starts, and Hive Mind reports the Formal AI version it actually ran.\n2. Either a pull request with a working Hello World program, or a failure that is **reported as a failure**:\n   - no \"✅ Work session finished successfully\" over a failed or empty session (#2303);\n   - no auto-restart loop over Formal AI's own files (#3248);\n   - no junk files (`e.g`, derivation records) in any commit;\n   - the complete session log is attached, or linked when it is too large.\n3. Nothing is closed that the run did not fix (#3276).\n4. The Formal AI image is removed or kept within its size budget after the session (#3207). Disk use returns to the pre-run baseline (about 45–49 GB on the current host).\n5. The run's logs are uploaded to private gists and linked here, after `$ --list` and `$ --status` confirm the task and its result.\n\nParent: #3215.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278","id":5852728778,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNmNyg","number":3278,"title":"Finish #3206: 123 baselined sync calls in bot modules, require-exec-timeout blind to $ calls, inline commands guarded only by a warning","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Why\n\n#3206 asked that installing or pulling Formal AI never blocks the Telegram bot, and that **every** synchronous operation that can be asynchronous is replaced, with lint rules so the harmful patterns cannot come back. #3225 delivered the main part, and listed what is left under \"Known limitations\":\n\n- The lint baseline still allows **123 sync calls** in modules the bot loads, including `state-lock` and the session snapshot write.\n- `require-exec-timeout` does not see `$` (command-stream) calls, so an unbounded `$` call in the bot is not reported.\n- `/help`, `/start`, `/top`, `/tokens`, `/queue`, `/language` and `/subscribe` still run inline. They have no slow step today, and the 2 s watchdog only warns if one gets one.\n\nThe rule set proposed for this is in https://gist.github.com/konard/e621dc37520a2ab7e64a006f0832e3c7.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Replace each of the 123 baselined sync calls with its async form, or keep it with an inline justification that the rule can read (for example module-load-time config read). Shrink the baseline to the justified ones.\n- [ ] Teach `require-exec-timeout` the `$` tagged template and `$({…})` forms of `command-stream`.\n- [ ] Make the watchdog a test failure, not only a runtime warning: a CI test that runs every bot command against a stubbed slow dependency and fails if the handler blocks the event loop for more than the budget.\n- [ ] Report the general rules to the linting dependency we use, if it lacks them (no such rule set exists upstream, per the gist).\n\n## Done when\n\n- The baseline holds only justified entries, each with its reason.\n- A deliberately added `execSync`, `readFileSync` in a handler, or an unbounded `$` call fails `npm run lint` in CI.\n\nParent: #3215.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279","id":5852729439,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNmQXw","number":3279,"title":"Formal AI parity across tools: commit attribution works only with --tool agent, cost needs a per-tool override","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391192,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6mA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Why\n\nFormal AI must be supported at every level, the same way as OpenAI and Anthropic models: through `/claude`, `/codex` and `/agent`. #3225's \"Known limitations\" lists two gaps where only `/agent` gets full support:\n\n- **Commit attribution** (`--attribution`, #2229) reads the agent's event stream, so it works only with `--tool agent`. Claude Code and Codex sessions on Formal AI get no trailers and no evidence bundle.\n- **Cost:** each tool has its own $0 override for Formal AI. Claude Code reports Anthropic list prices for any non-Anthropic `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, and only the Formal AI case is corrected.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Derive attribution for `--tool claude` (from its stream-json output) and `--tool codex` (from its JSONL events), with the same four trailers and evidence bundle as `--tool agent`.\n- [ ] Put the price for a non-Anthropic or non-OpenAI base URL in one place, keyed by the served model, instead of a per-tool override.\n- [ ] Add one test matrix: tool × {Anthropic, OpenAI, Formal AI}, asserting attribution, cost, model name and log attachment are reported the same way.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The matrix test passes, and a Formal AI run through each client produces the same trailers and a correct $0 cost.\n\nParent: #3215.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276","id":5852684068,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNjfJA","number":3276,"title":"Link repair follows sub-issues into other repositories: merging #3225 closed 11 formal-ai issues nothing had fixed","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391179,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6iw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:43:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:47:48Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nMerging #3225 closed **11 formal-ai issues that nothing had fixed**: link-assistant/formal-ai#1207, link-assistant/formal-ai#1189, link-assistant/formal-ai#1201, link-assistant/formal-ai#1203, link-assistant/formal-ai#1204, link-assistant/formal-ai#1205, link-assistant/formal-ai#1206, link-assistant/formal-ai#1208, link-assistant/formal-ai#1209, link-assistant/formal-ai#1210 and link-assistant/formal-ai#1211, all at 2026-10-14T17:11:41–48Z. formal-ai `main` has no commit after v0.353.2 (`8d2430d5c`, 2026-10-13), and #3225's own description lists \"formal-ai#1189, #1205–#1207, #1209 and #1211\" as the Formal AI issues that **remain open upstream**. They were reopened by hand on 2026-10-15. (link-assistant/formal-ai#1153 was delivered, because the slim image is published and Hive Mind prefers it, so it stays closed.)\n\nThis is the bug class of #3174, in its cross-repository form. It is worse there, because the other repository's maintainers see their issues closed by a merge in a repository they do not watch.\n\n## How it happened\n\n- #3215 (the source issue of #3225) had link-assistant/formal-ai#1207 as a native sub-issue, and #1207 has 11 sub-issues in formal-ai.\n- [`fetchRequiredIssueScope`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/d0084ee/src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs#L35-L55) walks the whole sub-issue tree, **including nodes in other repositories** (`normalizeSubIssueEntry` keeps their owner/repo), and marks every node as required.\n- [`repairRequiredIssueLinks`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/d0084ee/src/pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs#L18-L44) appended `Fixes link-assistant/formal-ai#N` for each of them ([L32](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/d0084ee/src/pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs#L32)). That is lines 97–119 of #3225's description, after the agent's own `Fixes` line, which named only hive-mind issues.\n- GitHub closes issues in other repositories of the same owner on merge. So the merge closed all 11.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Never require or add a closing reference for an issue in another repository.** A pull request can only fix code in its own repository. Walk sub-issues in other repositories for context, but never add them to the required scope.\n2. Respect a description that says an issue stays open, as #3174 asks. A `Fixes` line the repair added must be removed again when the description lists that issue as remaining open.\n3. Before any merge (auto or by command), compare `closingIssuesReferences` with what the PR implements. Refuse to merge, with a comment naming them, when it would close an issue in another repository.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A unit test reproduces this tree (#3215 → formal-ai#1207 → 11 formal-ai sub-issues): `repairRequiredIssueLinks` adds no `Fixes owner/other-repo#N` line, and the merge guard refuses a PR whose `closingIssuesReferences` contain another repository's issue.\n- Cross-repository sub-issues can be attached to umbrellas again without risk. Until then, umbrellas here link other repositories' issues only in their text.\n\nParent: #3174.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/3295","id":4862219792,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABIc-WEA","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/3295","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/3295.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/3295.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3295","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/3295/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/3295/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://a