d/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Summary\n\nAn automatic session-kill recovery ran the **Telegram command alias** as a shell command inside the resumed container, so the recovery died immediately:\n\n```\n$ docker logs e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b-resume-1\n[dind-entrypoint] Starting dockerd (storage-driver=fuse-overlayfs, data-root=/var/lib/docker)\n[dind-entrypoint] dockerd is ready after 1s\n[dind-entrypoint] image preload/passthrough complete\nsh: 1: /claude: not found                                  # exit 127\n```\n\n```\n$ docker inspect -f '{{json .Config.Cmd}}' e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b-resume-1\n[\"sh\",\"-c\",\"/claude https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 --think high --tool claude --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en --resume 41cebf9b-7516-44c0-8422-5bbafe26cee9\"]\n```\n\nSide effects:\n- The killed task (link-assistant/hive-mind#2591 / PR #2592) was **never resumed**. Its work survives only on `recovery/issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2`.\n- start-command's in-place resume ran `docker commit` on the stopped container, which left an image `start-command-resume/e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b:1` with **4.43 GB unique size**. It also left a stopped container `…-resume-1`. `hive-cleanup` sees neither (see #2629).\n\n## Timeline (UTC, 2026-10-07; hive-mind 2.33.11, start-command 0.35.1)\n\n| Time | Event |\n|---|---|\n| 09:07:42 | Task started from Telegram `/claude https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 --think high` in container `e6c1dd3f-…` (`d9a38c244727`), memory limit 2.92 GiB |\n| ~09:40 | `claude` killed: `CLAUDE execution failed with Claude command failed with exit code 137`; Docker `OOMKilled=true`. Failure comment: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2592#issuecomment-6035301295 (also referenced in #2613) |\n| 09:42:47 | Container exits 1. Uncommitted work is pushed to `recovery/issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2` |\n| 09:54:08 | Session-kill recovery: `$ --resume e6c1dd3f-… -- \"/claude … --resume 41cebf9b-…\"` → `docker commit` → container `e6c1dd3f-…-resume-1` |\n| 09:54:13 | `sh: 1: /claude: not found`, exit 127. No further attempt |\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/session-resume.lib.mjs` → `buildResumeCommand()` (same on `main`, line 264):\n\n```js\nconst commandAlias = typeof sessionInfo.commandAlias === 'string' && /^[a-z0-9_-]+$/i.test(sessionInfo.commandAlias) ? sessionInfo.commandAlias : null;\nconst bin = binary || (commandAlias ? `/${commandAlias}` : command);\n...\nreturn { binary: bin, args, display: `${bin} ${args.map(quoteArg).join(' ')}` };\n```\n\n`/${commandAlias}` is a *Telegram* command (`/claude`, `/codex`, ...), meant only for the \"♻️ Resume from last session\" chat message. But `src/session-kill-resume.in-place.lib.mjs` (line 197 on `main`) executes that display string:\n\n```js\nconst result = await runner.resumeIsolatedSession(decision.identifier, { command: plan?.command?.display || null, verbose });\n```\n\nSo every in-place recovery of a task started through a Telegram alias (`/claude`, `/codex`, `/agent`, ...) is broken, while tasks started with `/solve` work.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. Keep two fields in `buildResumeCommand()`. One is the executable command: `binary` = `solve` (or the persisted real command), with the args. The other is the chat text: `chatDisplay` = `/${commandAlias} …`. Pass only the executable one to `resumeIsolatedSession()`. The alias's implied options are already in `sessionInfo.args` (`--tool claude` is present above).\n2. Before calling `$ --resume … -- <command>`, assert that the first word of the command resolves inside the image (`command -v solve`), or use the absolute `exec 'solve' …` form that the original start command uses.\n3. Treat a recovery that exits **127 or 126 within seconds** as a failed recovery. Report it on the PR/issue and in Telegram (\"automatic recovery could not start: …\") instead of silently stopping. Retry with the fresh-launch path (`executeWithIsolation`) that `session-kill-resume.lib.mjs` already has.\n4. When a snapshot resume fails, remove the derived `-resume-N` container and its `start-command-resume/<uuid>:<n>` image, or at least report them. Otherwise each failed recovery leaks a full writable-layer copy (4.4 GB here).\n\n## Tests to add\n\n- `buildResumeCommand({ sessionInfo: { command: 'solve', commandAlias: 'claude', args: [url, '--tool', 'claude'] }, lastSessionId })`: the executable command must start with `solve` and the display may start with `/claude`.\n- An in-place resume plan built for an alias-launched session must not contain a leading `/` word in the command passed to `resumeIsolatedSession`.\n\n## Workaround\n\nResume manually: `$ --resume e6c1dd3f-3acd-475d-8df4-f45b75879a8b -- \"solve https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 --think high --tool claude --attach-logs --verbose --no-tool-check --disable-report-issue --language en --resume 41cebf9b-7516-44c0-8422-5bbafe26cee9\"`, or continue from branch `recovery/issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2`.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2630/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent/issues/332","id":5842317139,"node_id":"I_kwDOQYTy3M8AAAABXDqvUw","number":332,"title":"A recoverable failed tool call is emitted as a fatal top-level {\"type\":\"error\"} event, so Hive Mind fails the whole run","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2