t/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/deployments","created_at":"2025-11-18T18:30:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T14:16:47Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T14:19:49Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/agent.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/agent.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/agent","homepage":null,"size":13666,"stargazers_count":9,"watchers_count":9,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":4,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":4,"watchers":9,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Problem\n\nA tool call that fails and is *recovered from* is emitted as a top-level `{\"type\":\"error\"}` event, the same event type used for fatal session errors. Consumers cannot tell \"the model asked for a missing file and got an error result\" from \"the session failed\".\n\n`js/src/cli/event-handler.js` (main, 1197d6c):\n\n```js\nif (part.type === 'tool') {\n  eventHandler.output({ type: 'tool_use', ..., part });\n  // If tool failed, also output an error event\n  if (part.state?.status === 'error') {\n    eventHandler.output({ type: 'error', ..., part, message: errorText(stateError, 'Tool execution failed'), error: stateError || 'Tool execution failed' });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe `tool_use` event already carries `part.state.status === \"error\"` and the error text, so the extra top-level event only duplicates it, under the fatal type.\n\n## Impact (observed 2026-10-13, agent 0.26.13, Hive Mind 2.35.8)\n\n`/agent https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/issues/1 --model formal-ai`, execution `05c82f00-9417-4ebb-8c8c-97f2b893dd00`:\n\n- The model called `read` on `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-…/e.g` (formal-ai bug link-assistant/formal-ai#1189). The tool returned `File not found`, which is a normal, recoverable tool result.\n- agent emitted a top-level `type:\"error\"` event for it.\n- Hive Mind (`src/agent.lib.mjs` streaming detection, `src/agent-command.lib.mjs` `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery`, issue link-assistant/hive-mind#1201 logic) treats any top-level error event as fatal: *\"Agent exited 0 after an error event; the error event in its output still fails the run\"*. The run failed with `❌ AGENT execution failed with Agent reported error: Error: File not found: …/e.g`.\n\nThis affects every model, not only Formal AI: any recoverable tool error (a missing file, a non-zero `bash` exit with `--fail` semantics, a bad edit anchor) fails the whole Hive Mind run, and the reported reason names the tool error instead of the real outcome.\n\nLog (private gist, sanitized): https://gist.github.com/konard/a26a79ab44357a50859a51ff7f762af6\n\n## Expected\n\n- A failed tool call is reported only on its `tool_use` event (`part.state.status: \"error\"`), or, if a separate event is kept, with a distinct type such as `tool_error`, or `type:\"error\"` with `\"recoverable\": true` / `\"scope\": \"tool\"`.\n- `type:\"error\"` without a recoverable flag is reserved for errors that end the session or turn.\n- Document the contract in the JSON event docs so consumers (Hive Mind) can rely on it, and add a test: a session in which a tool fails and the model continues must not contain a fatal `error` event.\n\nHive Mind side: link-assistant/hive-mind#3213 (umbrella link-assistant/hive-mind#3215).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/agent/issues/332/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248","id":5844603295,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXF2Rnw","number":3248,"title":"Formal AI Draft workflow fails on every new issue (53/60 runs since 2026-10-07): a failed 'e.g' read fails the run; no-op drafts; false 'log not attached'; Formal AI cache pushed as recovery branches","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T08:34:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:41Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"repository":{"id":1027945641,"node_id":"R_kgDOPUU0qQ","name":"hive-mind","full_name":"link-assistant/hive-mind","private":false,"owner":{"login":"link-assistant","id":245352401,"node_id":"O_kgDODp_H0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245352401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","description":"The AI that controls AIs to do the automation of automation.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Summary\n\n`Formal AI Draft` (`.github/workflows/formal-ai-draft.yml`, triggered by `issues: opened`) **failed on 53 of the last 60 issue-triggered runs** (2026-10-07 → 2026-10-14). The other 7 runs were skipped by the `no-formal-ai-draft` label. No issue got a usable draft.\n\n| Cause | Runs |\n|---|---|\n| `❌ Agent reported error: Error: File not found: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-…/e.g` | **51** |\n| `docker run` exit 125: Docker Hub auth timeout while pulling `konard/hive-mind:latest` ([37993992264](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/37993992264), [37993481615](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/37993481615)) | 2 |\n\nLatest run: [38515996193](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/38515996193) (issue #3215, draft PR #3225, solve v2.35.9, formal-ai 0.353.1). First run in the sample: [37691785246](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/37691785246).\n\n## Root cause (verified in the run logs)\n\nThe failure is a chain of three defects. Each one alone would turn a failed tool call into a failed run:\n\n1. **Formal AI** treats the abbreviation in \"(e.g., returns empty content…)\" in Hive Mind's system prompt as a file. Its first action in every run is `Let me open e.g and read what it says.`, then `read /tmp/gh-issue-solver-…/e.g` → `File not found`. Temperature is 0, so this is deterministic. → link-assistant/formal-ai#1189\n2. **agent** emits that recoverable tool failure as a top-level `{\"type\":\"error\"}` event. → link-assistant/agent#332, **fixed in agent 0.26.14** (released 2026-10-14 07:01Z; verified below).\n3. **solve** fails the run on any error record in the output, even when the agent continued, completed and exited 0:\n   - log line: `ℹ️ Agent exited 0 after an error event; the error event in its output still fails the run`\n   - code: `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery` in `src/agent-command.lib.mjs:116-122`, by design since #1201\n   - → #3213\n\nHow it played out by version:\n- **0.352.1 (41 runs):** Formal AI stopped right after the error and asked `Reply \\`Report issue\\`` (formal-ai#1205).\n- **0.353.1 (10 runs):** Formal AI recovered and kept working (gh issue view, webfetch, bash), and solve then failed the run anyway because of step 3.\n\n**Even with all three fixed, the draft would still produce nothing.** Formal AI 0.353.1 ends with `terminal_state \"planned_not_executed\"`, and its goal is Hive Mind's entire prompt rather than the issue (link-assistant/formal-ai#1209, a regression of formal-ai#1064). Hive Mind would then report the run as a success with no change made (#3211).\n\n## Live re-check: run [38536131210](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/38536131210) (this issue, PR #3249, 2026-10-14 08:35Z)\n\nAt start, the runtime updater moved agent from 0.26.13 to 0.26.14 (`agentic-cli-updater: 1 updated`). The `e.g` read failed again, but it was **no longer a fatal error event**, and the session went on. It then hit the next blockers:\n\n- **Formal AI 0.353.1 created garbage files.** It wrote `e.g` and `formal-ai-draft.yml` into the repo root, filled with the fetched GitHub page text, and said \"Created and verified\" (link-assistant/formal-ai#1211).\n- **Restart loop.** The untracked `e.g`, `formal-ai-draft.yml` and `data/cache/` (formal-ai#1208) triggered **`--auto-restart-on-uncommitted-changes` 5 of 5 times**:\n  - 18 PR comments, 7 `Add development log` commits, 28 min (08:37 → 09:05);\n  - then `❌ Auto-restart limit reached` and another `recovery/issue-3248-…` branch.\n- **Broken command on every restart.** Each restart ran `gh pr view … --comments --json comments,reviews`, which gh rejects (exit 1), then stopped (formal-ai#1158 comment).\n- **The log link works on this path.** The comment `📎 Log file uploaded as Repository` links the committed `solve.log`. Only the failure-comment path (item 3) is wrong.\n\n## Proposed fixes in Hive Mind\n\n1. **Tool errors are not run errors (#3213).** In `resolveStreamingErrorRecovery` and the output error detection, classify an error record whose part is a tool call (`part.type === 'tool'` with `part.state.status === 'error'`) as recoverable. Fail only on session or provider errors that no later completion follows, or on a non-zero exit. Add a test from run 38515996193's stream: `read e.g` fails, the session continues, exit 0 → not failed on that error.\n2. **A draft that changes nothing is a failure, with the reason given (#3211).** After the session, if the branch has no commits beyond `Initial commit with task details` and the development log, end with \"Formal AI produced no change\" plus Formal AI's terminal state (for example `planned_not_executed`). It must not be \"success\", and not the unrelated first tool error either.\n3. **The failure comment must point to the log that exists.**\n   - **What happened:**\n     - The PR #3225 comment (05:31:44Z) says `⚠️ Log Upload Failed … not attached here` (`gh-upload-log`: HTTP 403, a workflow `GITHUB_TOKEN` cannot create gists).\n     - It points to `/home/box/logs/solve-….log` inside a `docker run --rm` container that no longer exists.\n     - Yet two seconds later (05:31:46Z) `--development-log` committed the **complete** log: `dev/log/issues/3215/pulls/3225/sessions/…/solve.log`, 1,095,066 bytes.\n     - The workflow artifact `formal-ai-draft-session-3215` was uploaded too.\n   - **Fix:**\n     - Commit the development log before writing the comment, and link that file.\n     - When running in Actions, also link the run's artifact (`$GITHUB_SERVER_URL/$GITHUB_REPOSITORY/actions/runs/$GITHUB_RUN_ID`).\n     - Never print a container path for a `--rm` container.\n   - **Code:** `src/log-upload-failure.lib.mjs:84`, `src/log-upload.lib.mjs:373`.\n4. **Don't preserve Formal AI's own state as user work.**\n   - **What happened:** on 0.353.1, Formal AI writes `data/cache/derivations/answer_*.lino` into the workspace (link-assistant/formal-ai#1208). `commitUncommittedChangesOnCriticalError` (`src/critical-error-commit.lib.mjs`) then pushed them as **10 branches** `recovery/issue-3206-…` to `recovery/issue-3215-…`, which hold nothing else.\n   - **Fix:**\n     - Start the task-owned `formal-ai serve` with a cwd outside the repository and with `FORMAL_AI_CACHE_DIR` set to the session's own cache.\n     - Skip `data/cache/derivations/` and `.formal-ai/` in the preservation step, the same way build output is skipped already.\n     - Delete the 10 junk recovery branches once confirmed.\n5. **Pull the image with retries, and pin it.**\n   - Pull before `docker run` with retries and backoff, since 2 runs died on a single registry timeout.\n   - Use the image of the version in the checked-out `package.json` instead of `:latest`. Then the workflow scripts and the image always match, and a run is reproducible.\n   - The pull takes ~5 min of each run (05:22:42Z → 05:27:33Z in 38515996193).\n6. **Make the draft's checks visible on the PR.** PR #3225 shows only CodeQL:\n   - its `pull_request` runs (Checks and release, Security) wait in `action_required`;\n   - the dispatched runs (e.g. [38517135151](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/actions/runs/38517135151), success) are not attached to the PR.\n   - Fix: post the dispatched results as commit statuses on the head SHA, or as a summary comment.\n7. **Turn off the uncommitted-changes restart for drafts.** `DRAFT_SOLVE_FLAGS` (`scripts/formal-ai-draft.lib.mjs:86`) turns off `--auto-restart-until-mergeable` to keep one attempt per run. It leaves `--auto-restart-on-uncommitted-changes` on (default true, `src/solve.config.lib.mjs:244`), so the \"solve's own restart loop is disabled\" comment in `formal-ai-draft.yml` is not true.\n   - Add `--no-auto-restart-on-uncommitted-changes` and cover it in `tests/formal-ai-draft-2233.test.mjs`.\n   - In general (Telegram too), files the tool itself writes for its own state (`data/cache/derivations/`, `.formal-ai/`) should not count as \"uncommitted changes\" that restart the model.\n8. **Reuse:** add `workflow_call` to `formal-ai-draft.yml`, with inputs for the image and the Formal AI binary source, so link-assistant/formal-ai can run the same workflow on its own issues (link-assistant/formal-ai#1210).\n\n## Backlog the failing runs left\n\nOpen now in this repository:\n- **15** open draft `[WIP]` PRs by `app/github-actions` from these drafts (45 open PRs by that author in total);\n- **11** `recovery/*` branches, 10 of them from the 2026-10-14 drafts;\n- for scale: 1406 `issue-*` branches from all solve runs, not only drafts.\n\nThe daily `health` job reports attempts, but nothing flags that 100% of them fail for one known reason.\n\nSuggestion: the health job fails when the same `decision_code` or first error repeats N times in a row, and names the tracking issue.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA newly opened issue in this repository gets a draft run where:\n- a failed tool call does not end the run;\n- a run that changes nothing is reported as failed, with Formal AI's terminal state as the reason;\n- the failure comment links the complete log (committed file and/or artifact);\n- no `recovery/*` branch holds Formal AI cache files;\n- an image pull failure is retried.\n\nParent: #3215. Related: #2233, #1201, #3211, #3213, link-assistant/agent#332, link-assistant/formal-ai#1189, #1205, #1208, #1209, #1210, #1211, #1158.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3248/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3277","id":5852728229,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNmLpQ","number":3277,"title":"Live verification of #3215 after deploying 2.35.10: Formal AI Hello World through /claude, /codex and /agent on a host with no cached image","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/re