ive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Why\n\n#3206 asked that installing or pulling Formal AI never blocks the Telegram bot, and that **every** synchronous operation that can be asynchronous is replaced, with lint rules so the harmful patterns cannot come back. #3225 delivered the main part, and listed what is left under \"Known limitations\":\n\n- The lint baseline still allows **123 sync calls** in modules the bot loads, including `state-lock` and the session snapshot write.\n- `require-exec-timeout` does not see `$` (command-stream) calls, so an unbounded `$` call in the bot is not reported.\n- `/help`, `/start`, `/top`, `/tokens`, `/queue`, `/language` and `/subscribe` still run inline. They have no slow step today, and the 2 s watchdog only warns if one gets one.\n\nThe rule set proposed for this is in https://gist.github.com/konard/e621dc37520a2ab7e64a006f0832e3c7.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Replace each of the 123 baselined sync calls with its async form, or keep it with an inline justification that the rule can read (for example module-load-time config read). Shrink the baseline to the justified ones.\n- [ ] Teach `require-exec-timeout` the `$` tagged template and `$({…})` forms of `command-stream`.\n- [ ] Make the watchdog a test failure, not only a runtime warning: a CI test that runs every bot command against a stubbed slow dependency and fails if the handler blocks the event loop for more than the budget.\n- [ ] Report the general rules to the linting dependency we use, if it lacks them (no such rule set exists upstream, per the gist).\n\n## Done when\n\n- The baseline holds only justified entries, each with its reason.\n- A deliberately added `execSync`, `readFileSync` in a handler, or an unbounded `$` call fails `npm run lint` in CI.\n\nParent: #3215.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3278/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279","id":5852729439,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNmQXw","number":3279,"title":"Formal AI parity across tools: commit attribution works only with --tool agent, cost needs a per-tool override","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9018391192,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAACGYm6mA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:46:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3215","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"repository":{"id":1027945641,"node_id":"R_kgDOPUU0qQ","name":"hive-mind","full_name":"link-assistant/hive-mind","private":false,"owner":{"login":"link-assistant","id":245352401,"node_id":"O_kgDODp_H0Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245352401?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-assistant/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","description":"The AI that controls AIs to do the automation of automation.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/deployments","created_at":"2025-07-28T19:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:22:27Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:39Z","git_url":"git://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:link-assistant/hive-mind.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind","homepage":"","size":496236,"stargazers_count":89,"watchers_count":89,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":17,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":273,"license":{"key":"unlicense","name":"The Unlicense","spdx_id":"Unlicense","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/unlicense","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE1"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":17,"open_issues":273,"watchers":89,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":false}},"body":"## Why\n\nFormal AI must be supported at every level, the same way as OpenAI and Anthropic models: through `/claude`, `/codex` and `/agent`. #3225's \"Known limitations\" lists two gaps where only `/agent` gets full support:\n\n- **Commit attribution** (`--attribution`, #2229) reads the agent's event stream, so it works only with `--tool agent`. Claude Code and Codex sessions on Formal AI get no trailers and no evidence bundle.\n- **Cost:** each tool has its own $0 override for Formal AI. Claude Code reports Anthropic list prices for any non-Anthropic `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, and only the Formal AI case is corrected.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Derive attribution for `--tool claude` (from its stream-json output) and `--tool codex` (from its JSONL events), with the same four trailers and evidence bundle as `--tool agent`.\n- [ ] Put the price for a non-Anthropic or non-OpenAI base URL in one place, keyed by the served model, instead of a per-tool override.\n- [ ] Add one test matrix: tool × {Anthropic, OpenAI, Formal AI}, asserting attribution, cost, model name and log attachment are reported the same way.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The matrix test passes, and a Formal AI run through each client produces the same trailers and a correct $0 cost.\n\nParent: #3215.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3279/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174","id":5825265290,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABWzZ-ig","number":3174,"title":"Post-session link repair adds Fixes for sub-issues a planning PR only created, and auto-merge closes them unimplemented","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-13T05:50:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T05:50:35Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":1,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3282","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\n`solve` treats every native sub-issue of the source issue as an issue the PR must close. When the source issue asks for a **plan** (analysis plus creating implementation issues), the session attaches the implementation issues as sub-issues. From then on the post-session repair appends `Fixes #N` for each of them after **every** session, even when the agent deliberately removed those lines. Auto-merge then closes issues that were never implemented.\n\nThat is what happened in link-assistant/calculator:\n\n- PR link-assistant/calculator#228 was the plan for link-assistant/calculator#227. Its description said: `Merging this PR closes only #227. The open sub-issues #236 to #246 stay open, so this description deliberately has no Fixes lines for them.`\n- The repair appended `Fixes #229` … `Fixes #246` at 2026-10-07T10:31:07Z. The agent removed them at 10:33:43Z, and the repair re-added them at 10:44:47Z.\n- On 2026-10-12 the agent removed them twice more (19:16:26Z and 19:23:12Z). The repair re-added them at 19:40:26Z.\n- hive-mind auto-merged at 19:44:21Z. GitHub then closed link-assistant/calculator#236 to link-assistant/calculator#246, which were not implemented. They have now been reopened by hand.\n- Before the merge, the same lines made `--skip-issues-with-prs` skip every open issue in the repository (link-assistant/calculator#247, #2685).\n\nThe full timeline, every description revision and the closed events are in [docs/case-studies/issue-247](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/1b91a43a/docs/case-studies/issue-247/README.md).\n\n## Root cause (at ed6a155, v2.35.8)\n\n1. [`fetchRequiredIssueScope`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs#L34-L53) walks `…/sub_issues` recursively ([L44](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs#L44)) and marks every node as required. Nothing separates \"sub-issues to implement\" from \"sub-issues created as the plan's output\".\n2. [`repairRequiredIssueLinks`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs#L18-L44) appends a `Fixes` line for each missing one ([L32](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs#L32)). It runs in the [`finally` block](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/solve.restart-shared.lib.mjs#L551-L555) after every session, so it always overrides the agent. It ignores a description that explicitly says the issue stays open.\n3. Auto-merge does not compare what GitHub will close (`closingIssuesReferences`) with what the PR implements.\n\n### Second problem: the shared parser and GitHub disagree on negation\n\n[`extractClosingIssueReferences`](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/ed6a15520e49aafd49c06b49733ae8c28a15c4a6/src/github-linking.lib.mjs#L38-L53) skips a keyword whose clause contains `not`, `never`, `won't` and so on. The comment there cites a PR body that said `does not close #322`. GitHub does not skip such keywords. On link-assistant/calculator#261, adding `Probe for #247: this pull request does not close #258.` made `gh pr view 261 --json closingIssuesReferences` return `[258, 260]`. Merging would have closed link-assistant/calculator#258. GitLab documents the same behaviour: https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitlab-foss/-/work_items/55970. So hive-mind's linking checks can say \"#N is not closed\" while the merge closes it.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe script below calls hive-mind's own `repairRequiredIssueLinks` and `extractClosingIssueReferences`, with a fake `gh` runner. It needs a checkout at ed6a155 with `npm ci --ignore-scripts --omit=dev`, then `node repro.mjs <checkout>`.\n\n<details><summary>repro.mjs</summary>\n\n```js\n// Reproduces link-assistant/calculator#247 against hive-mind's own modules.\n// Usage: node repro.mjs <path to hive-mind checkout>\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n\nconst src = (file) => pathToFileURL(resolve(process.argv[2], 'src', file)).href;\nconst { repairRequiredIssueLinks } = await import(src('pr-issue-link-repair.lib.mjs'));\nconst { extractClosingIssueReferences } = await import(src('github-linking.lib.mjs'));\n\n// #1 asks for a plan; #2 and #3 are the implementation issues the session\n// created and attached as native sub-issues.\nconst issues = {\n  1: \"Analyse the problem and create one issue per part of the work. This issue's own result is the analysis and the issue creation.\",\n  2: 'Implement part A.',\n  3: 'Implement part B.',\n};\nconst subIssues = { 1: [2, 3], 2: [], 3: [] };\nlet prBody = 'Closes #1\\n\\nThis PR only plans the work: #2 and #3 stay open.';\n\nconst ok = (value) => ({ code: 0, stdout: JSON.stringify(value), stderr: '' });\nconst run = async (args) => {\n  const [command, target] = args;\n  if (command === 'api' && /issues\\/\\d+\\/sub_issues$/.test(target)) {\n    const number = Number(target.split('/').at(-2));\n    return ok([subIssues[number].map((n) => ({ number: n, repository_url: 'https://api.github.com/repos/o/r' }))]);\n  }\n  if (command === 'api' && /issues\\/\\d+$/.test(target)) {\n    const number = Number(target.split('/').at(-1));\n    return ok({ number, body: issues[number] });\n  }\n  if (command === 'api' && /pulls\\/10$/.test(target)) return ok({ number: 10, body: prBody });\n  if (command === 'pr' && target === 'edit') {\n    prBody = readFileSync(args[args.indexOf('--body-file') + 1], 'utf8');\n    return { code: 0, stdout: '', stderr: '' };\n  }\n  throw new Error(`unexpected gh ${args.join(' ')}`);\n};\n\nconst repair = () => repairRequiredIssueLinks({ owner: 'o', repo: 'r', issueNumber: 1, prNumber: 10, run, logger: async (m) => console.log('  log:', m) });\n\nconsole.log('1. Session ends; the finally-block repair runs:');\nawait repair();\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(prBody));\n\nconsole.log('2. The next session removes the lines again; the repair re-adds them:');\nprBody = prBody.replace(/\\n\\n---\\n\\nFixes #2\\nFixes #3$/, '');\nawait repair();\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(prBody));\n\nconsole.log('3. hive-mind and GitHub disagree on negated keywords:');\nconst text = 'This PR does not close #2.';\nconsole.log(`  extractClosingIssueReferences(${JSON.stringify(text)}) =`, JSON.stringify(extractClosingIssueReferences(text)));\nconsole.log('  GitHub: closingIssuesReferences lists #2, and merging closes it (probe on link-assistant/calculator#261).');\n```\n\n</details>\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n1. Session ends; the finally-block repair runs:\n  log: 🔗 Repaired 2 required issue-closing reference(s) in PR #10.\n\"Closes #1\\n\\nThis PR only plans the work: #2 and #3 stay open.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFixes #2\\nFixes #3\"\n2. The next session removes the lines again; the repair re-adds them:\n  log: 🔗 Repaired 2 required issue-closing reference(s) in PR #10.\n\"Closes #1\\n\\nThis PR only plans the work: #2 and #3 stay open.\\n\\n---\\n\\nFixes #2\\nFixes #3\"\n3. hive-mind and GitHub disagree on negated keywords:\n  extractClosingIssueReferences(\"This PR does not close #2.\") = []\n  GitHub: closingIssuesReferences lists #2, and merging closes it (probe on link-assistant/calculator#261).\n```\n\n## Workarounds\n\n- In repositories hive-mind auto-merges, add a required check that fails when the description's closing keywords contradict its prose. link-assistant/calculator#261 adds one: [`scripts/check-closing-references.mjs`](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/1b91a43a/scripts/check-closing-references.mjs), run on `pull_request: [opened, edited, synchronize, reopened]`. With that check failing, hive-mind does not auto-merge.\n- For planning issues, run without auto-merge, and remove the appended lines by hand right before merging.\n- Do not write \"does not close #N\". Write \"#N stays open\" without a keyword.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n1. **Scope.** In `fetchRequiredIssueScope`, do not treat a native sub-issue as required when either of these holds:\n   - it was created after the PR was opened (plan output), or\n   - another PR already closes it (`closedByPullRequestsReferences`).\n\n   Keep the explicit repository-mode block (`parseRequiredClosingReferences`) and the current all-sub-issues behaviour when the parent asks for implementation, for example with an opt-in marker or flag.\n2. **Respect the description.** In `repairRequiredIssueLinks`, do not add `Fixes #N` when the body mentions `#N` without a keyword, for example in \"Part of #N\", \"#N stays open\" or \"#N to #M stay open\". Log it instead: `⚠️ #N is in the sub-issue tree but the description keeps it open; not adding a closing reference.`\n3. **Never undo the agent.** If the agent removed a reference the previous repair added, do not re-add it in the `finally` block. Report the conflict in the session summary instead.\n4. **Parser parity.** Make `extractClosingIssueReferences` return negated references, because GitHub closes them, and report them as errors (\"'does not close #N' still closes #N\"). Alternatively, use GraphQL `closingIssuesReferences` as the source of truth for repair, skip and merge checks. Before auto-merge, refuse when `closingIssuesReferences` includes an issue that is still open, is in the sub-issue tree, and has no commits in the PR (this overlaps #2406).\n5. **Regression test.** Use the link-assistant/calculator#227 wording (\"this issue's own result is the analysis and issue creation\") and assert that the implementation sub-issues created during the session are not added.\n\nRelated: #2685 / #2686 (the no-work report this caused), #2406 (complete delivery before auto-merge), #2615 (sub-issue and blocker awareness in `/hive`), #2891 (kill notices posted to the parent plan PR), link-assistant/calculator#247, link-assistant/calculator#260.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3174/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276/events","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3276","id":5852684068,"node_id":"I_kwDOPUU0qc8AAAABXNjfJA","number":3276,"title":"Link repair follows sub-issues into other repositories: mergin